WEBVTT

asr-000049a
00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:17.303
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Good morning, everyone. This briefing of the Development Budget Coordination Committee, or the DBCC, is hereby called to order. Please rise for the singing of the national anthem and please remain standing for the opening prayer to be led by Vice Chairperson Johanne Bautista of the TRABAHO Party-list.

asr-000049b
00:17:17.303 --> 00:17:48.893
House ceremonial singers: [National anthem performed]

asr-000049c
00:18:29.528 --> 00:19:51.203
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Let us put ourselves in the presence of Almighty God. Ever-living God, we bow our heads before You today with hearts full of gratitude and profound responsibility as we begin our budget briefing. Grant us, Lord, the wisdom, discernment, and steadfast dedication needed to craft a national budget that truly serves the Filipino people, a budget that drives economic recovery, creates sustainable and decent livelihoods, and uplifts every worker, family, and community across our archipelago. Lord God of creation, we also place before Your loving protection the Filipino people, especially as our nation faces the trials of inclement weather and natural calamities. We ask for Your merciful mantle of safety and security to shield every community, home, and vulnerable family. Please grant strength and resilience to our frontline workers, local leaders, and disaster response teams, and guide our hands to allocate the resources necessary to protect, prepare, and deliver swift aid to those in need. May everything we discuss and decide today and in the next few weeks be guided by integrity, compassion, and unwavering commitment to public service and the common good. Amen.

asr-000049d
00:19:59.945 --> 00:20:08.180
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you, Honorable Johanne Bautista. ComSec, please acknowledge the members and resource persons present in today's briefing.

