asr-000212
00:35:43.040 --> 00:36:02.540
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Consistent with our mandate, we worry about inflation because it diminishes the purchasing power of Filipino families. Low inflation also supports sustainable growth. We are encouraged to report that

asr-000213
00:36:03.740 --> 00:36:12.620
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: inflation has eased somewhat over the last 3 months. However, inflation remains well above

asr-000217
00:36:13.020 --> 00:36:21.260
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: this is due largely to global supply shocks and their spillover effects on prices in the domestic

asr-000218
00:36:21.260 --> 00:36:30.540
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: economy as you know oil price shocks are are not just about energy they are also about food prices

asr-000219
00:36:31.260 --> 00:36:35.180
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: because oil is also the source of much of our fertilizer

asr-000220
00:36:35.180 --> 00:36:44.220
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: to contain price pressures the bsp has responded by tightening monetary policy

asr-000221
00:36:44.860 --> 00:36:53.420
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: twice this year these were carefully calibrated moves to help slow down inflation

asr-000222
00:36:54.540 --> 00:37:01.020
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: anchor inflation expectations while recognizing the temporary weakness in growth

asr-000223
00:37:03.100 --> 00:37:05.100
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: over the medium term we expect inflation to increase

asr-000224
00:37:05.980 --> 00:37:16.380
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: gradually however risks remain tilted to the upside the monetary board will meet next week

asr-000225
00:37:17.100 --> 00:37:24.700
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: to decide on the next policy action we look at all the evidence and we are prepared

asr-000226
00:37:24.700 --> 00:37:31.180
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: to take further steps as necessary to ensure that inflation returns to target

asr-000227
00:37:33.420 --> 00:37:34.860
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: i'm also glad to report

asr-000228
00:37:35.820 --> 00:37:41.740
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: that the philippine banking system remains well provisioned and well capitalized

asr-000229
00:37:43.100 --> 00:37:51.260
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: banks are also flush with liquidity they are well positioned to continue to support economic activity

asr-000230
00:37:52.780 --> 00:38:00.940
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: our strong external position also provides an important buffer against global uncertainties

asr-000231
00:38:03.260 --> 00:38:04.860
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: this macroeconomic backdrop

asr-000232
00:38:05.580 --> 00:38:11.740
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: supports the assumptions behind the proposed national government budget for 2027.

asr-000233
00:38:13.500 --> 00:38:20.220
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: with that let me turn the floor over to deputy governor zeno Abenoja who will provide a more

asr-000234
00:38:20.220 --> 00:38:26.540
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: detailed overview of the macroeconomic developments and assumptions thank you

asr-000235
00:38:28.620 --> 00:38:32.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: thank you governor i joined the governor in

asr-000236
00:38:32.380 --> 00:38:43.260
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the last minutes uh saying our thanks to our honorable speaker Speaker Bodjie Dy III our

asr-000237
00:38:43.260 --> 00:38:50.700
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: honorable chair Congresswoman Mikaela Angela Suansing and our honorable representatives present

asr-000238
00:38:50.700 --> 00:38:56.460
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: at today's briefing the bsp is a resource institution of the dbcc

asr-000239
00:38:57.260 --> 00:38:57.980
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and for this morning we will provide some context for the macroeconomic

asr-000240
00:38:57.980 --> 00:39:01.820
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: this morning we will provide some context for the macroeconomic developments and assumptions

asr-000241
00:39:02.380 --> 00:39:09.100
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: assumptions behind the proposed national government budget for the fiscal year 2027.

asr-000242
00:39:09.980 --> 00:39:15.900
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: So let me start with some brief overview of what is happening in the economy.

asr-000243
00:39:16.780 --> 00:39:26.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: What is the latest trend in terms of inflation? In 2025, we see here that lower food, particularly

asr-000244
00:39:26.380 --> 00:39:35.100
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: rice and energy prices significantly eased the country's inflation. This continued in the first

asr-000245
00:39:35.100 --> 00:39:42.060
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: two months of this year, 2026. However, the conflict in the Middle East since end February

asr-000246
00:39:42.060 --> 00:39:49.660
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: 2026 drove global oil prices higher, and this translated to significant spillover

asr-000247
00:39:49.660 --> 00:39:55.660
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to domestic inflation. Inflation rose from 2.4%

asr-000248
00:39:56.860 --> 00:40:07.180
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: in February of this year to a recent peak at 7.2% in April. However, since then, it has gradually

asr-000249
00:40:07.180 --> 00:40:17.260
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: eased to 6.2% by July. However, that number, that inflation number, continued to be well

asr-000250
00:40:17.260 --> 00:40:25.980
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: above the target of 3%. The moderation that we have seen since the period May to July

asr-000251
00:40:26.380 --> 00:40:33.580
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: in inflation reflects lower global oil prices and improve food supply conditions.

asr-000252
00:40:34.940 --> 00:40:37.180
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: What was the response of the BSP?

asr-000253
00:40:38.380 --> 00:40:45.820
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: As the Governor has mentioned, monetary policy shifted to a tightening stance with this rise in

asr-000254
00:40:45.820 --> 00:40:55.900
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: inflation, and also the increase in the inflation outlook. The BSP decided to raise target policy rates,

asr-000255
00:40:56.380 --> 00:41:05.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: from 4.25% by 25 basis points each in April and June 2026.

asr-000256
00:41:05.380 --> 00:41:10.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This brings the policy rate to 4.75%.

asr-000257
00:41:10.380 --> 00:41:17.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This calibrated move by the BSP helps anchor inflation expectations

asr-000258
00:41:17.380 --> 00:41:21.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and reduce what we call second round risks.

asr-000259
00:41:21.380 --> 00:41:28.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: At the same time, this measured policy action supports growth.

asr-000260
00:41:28.380 --> 00:41:33.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The calibrated monetary policy action will complement fiscal measures

asr-000261
00:41:33.380 --> 00:41:38.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: in supporting steady consumption and strengthening business sentiment.

asr-000262
00:41:38.380 --> 00:41:44.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: In the coming months, in the coming quarters, amid the challenging external environment,

asr-000263
00:41:44.380 --> 00:41:47.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the BSP will remain data dependent.

asr-000264
00:41:47.380 --> 00:41:51.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The BSP will remain vigilant and prepared to take first steps

asr-000265
00:41:51.380 --> 00:41:55.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to further monetary actions to ensure that inflation returns

asr-000266
00:41:55.380 --> 00:42:00.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to the target of 3% over the medium term.

asr-000267
00:42:00.380 --> 00:42:07.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Where do we see inflation going this year and next year in 2027?

asr-000268
00:42:07.380 --> 00:42:14.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The inflation outlook has deteriorated amid the challenging external environment

asr-000269
00:42:14.380 --> 00:42:20.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and amid the faster than expected broadening of price pressure.

asr-000270
00:42:20.380 --> 00:42:21.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: We can see this.

asr-000271
00:42:21.380 --> 00:42:25.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: We can tell from what we call core inflation numbers.

asr-000272
00:42:25.380 --> 00:42:28.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Our analysis point to stronger second round effects

asr-000273
00:42:28.380 --> 00:42:32.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and a wider pass-through of earlier supply shocks

asr-000274
00:42:32.380 --> 00:42:37.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to the different components of the consumption basket.

asr-000275
00:42:37.380 --> 00:42:40.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: In the monetary policy meeting last June,

asr-000276
00:42:40.380 --> 00:42:48.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the BSP sees headline inflation averaging at 6.4% in 2026,

asr-000277
00:42:48.380 --> 00:42:50.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: 4.5% in 2027,

asr-000278
00:42:50.380 --> 00:42:54.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and 4.5% in 2027.

asr-000279
00:42:54.380 --> 00:43:00.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And both numbers are above the inflation target of 3%.

asr-000280
00:43:00.380 --> 00:43:05.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: However, by 2028, it is possible that inflation will be close to the target

asr-000281
00:43:05.380 --> 00:43:09.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: at around 3.1%.

asr-000282
00:43:09.380 --> 00:43:13.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The BSP sees upside inflation risk,

asr-000283
00:43:13.380 --> 00:43:18.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and this could emanate largely from the higher global oil prices

asr-000284
00:43:18.380 --> 00:43:22.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and higher inflation expectations.

asr-000285
00:43:22.380 --> 00:43:25.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: If you look at private sector inflation forecasts,

asr-000286
00:43:25.380 --> 00:43:29.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: they could also see higher inflation in the near term.

asr-000287
00:43:29.380 --> 00:43:38.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: But this could revert to near the 3% level by 2028 or 2029.

asr-000288
00:43:38.380 --> 00:43:41.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Now going to the banking system,

asr-000289
00:43:41.380 --> 00:43:44.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: how is the banking system performing?

asr-000290
00:43:44.380 --> 00:43:47.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The banking system remains healthy.

asr-000291
00:43:48.380 --> 00:43:53.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The Philippine banking system is supported by strong fundamentals.

asr-000292
00:43:53.380 --> 00:43:57.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Banks sustain growth in assets and deposits

asr-000293
00:43:57.380 --> 00:44:00.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and continued profitability.

asr-000294
00:44:00.380 --> 00:44:05.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Capital and liquidity metrics remain well above international standards,

asr-000295
00:44:05.380 --> 00:44:10.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and non-performing loans are manageable and well provisioned.

asr-000296
00:44:10.380 --> 00:44:15.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Looking ahead, the banking system is well positioned

asr-000297
00:44:15.380 --> 00:44:17.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to support economic activity

asr-000298
00:44:17.380 --> 00:44:21.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and financial stability.

asr-000299
00:44:21.380 --> 00:44:24.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: We also observed that more Filipinos

asr-000300
00:44:24.380 --> 00:44:29.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: continue to participate in the formal financial system.

asr-000301
00:44:29.380 --> 00:44:33.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The chart on the left shows that digital payments

asr-000302
00:44:33.380 --> 00:44:39.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: reached almost 65% of retail transactions last year.

asr-000303
00:44:39.380 --> 00:44:45.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This surpasses the targets of 50% to 54%.

asr-000304
00:44:45.380 --> 00:44:47.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And our data shows even more.

asr-000305
00:44:47.380 --> 00:44:48.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: In the last few months,

asr-000306
00:44:48.380 --> 00:44:51.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: we have seen an increase in the number of payments

asr-000307
00:44:51.380 --> 00:44:54.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: that have been made through digital payments.

asr-000308
00:44:54.380 --> 00:44:57.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This is due to increasing use of payments

asr-000309
00:44:57.380 --> 00:45:01.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: through Instapay, Pesonet, and person-to-merchant QRPH.

asr-000310
00:45:01.380 --> 00:45:04.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This highlights the continued momentum

asr-000311
00:45:04.380 --> 00:45:08.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: on the adoption of electronic payments channels in the country.

asr-000312
00:45:08.380 --> 00:45:10.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Equally important,

asr-000313
00:45:10.380 --> 00:45:13.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the growing adoption of digital payments

asr-000314
00:45:13.380 --> 00:45:17.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: also generates what are called network externalities.

asr-000315
00:45:17.380 --> 00:45:20.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Electronic payment channels increase

asr-000316
00:45:20.380 --> 00:45:23.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: as more consumers, more merchants,

asr-000317
00:45:23.380 --> 00:45:26.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and more financial institutions participate

asr-000318
00:45:26.380 --> 00:45:31.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: in this financial ecosystem.

asr-000319
00:45:31.380 --> 00:45:33.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: On the right side,

asr-000320
00:45:33.380 --> 00:45:37.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: we show the increasing number of basic deposit accounts,

asr-000321
00:45:37.380 --> 00:45:43.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and it has reached over 28 million as of March 2026,

asr-000322
00:45:43.380 --> 00:45:46.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: with 177 banks offering basic deposits.

asr-000323
00:45:46.380 --> 00:45:49.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This is one of the ways

asr-000324
00:45:49.380 --> 00:45:54.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: that we at the BSP promote financial inclusion.

asr-000325
00:45:54.380 --> 00:45:57.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: We also welcome the decision of several banks

asr-000326
00:45:57.380 --> 00:46:03.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to reduce or waive interbank digital transaction fees.

asr-000327
00:46:03.380 --> 00:46:08.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This reduction or waiver of interbank digital transaction fees

asr-000328
00:46:08.380 --> 00:46:12.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: makes it more affordable and accessible

asr-000329
00:46:12.380 --> 00:46:15.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: for Filipino households and small businesses

asr-000330
00:46:15.380 --> 00:46:23.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to access the convenience of electronic fund transfers.

asr-000331
00:46:23.380 --> 00:46:25.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: We also thank our legislators

asr-000332
00:46:25.380 --> 00:46:29.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: for the passage of the Anti-Financial Accounts Coming Act.

asr-000333
00:46:29.380 --> 00:46:32.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This is indeed an important legislation

asr-000334
00:46:32.380 --> 00:46:35.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to continue to improve the consumer protection

asr-000335
00:46:35.380 --> 00:46:38.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: through stronger safeguards for fraud

asr-000336
00:46:38.380 --> 00:46:42.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and faster complaint resolutions.

asr-000337
00:46:42.380 --> 00:46:44.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: At the external front,

asr-000338
00:46:44.380 --> 00:46:47.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: if you look at our external sector,

asr-000339
00:46:47.380 --> 00:46:50.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: it continues to protect our economy

asr-000340
00:46:50.380 --> 00:46:54.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: from the effects of the volatile external conditions.

asr-000341
00:46:54.380 --> 00:46:57.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Right now, we have a balance of payments deficit

asr-000342
00:46:57.380 --> 00:47:01.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: of about 1.2% of GDP.

asr-000343
00:47:01.380 --> 00:47:03.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This is for last year,

asr-000344
00:47:03.380 --> 00:47:06.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and the current account narrowed

asr-000345
00:47:06.380 --> 00:47:09.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: due to strong exports and remittances.

asr-000346
00:47:09.380 --> 00:47:12.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: For 2026 and 2027,

asr-000347
00:47:12.380 --> 00:47:18.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the current account deficit is projected to slightly widen,

asr-000348
00:47:18.380 --> 00:47:20.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and this is consistent with the experience

asr-000349
00:47:20.380 --> 00:47:23.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: of many emerging market economies

asr-000350
00:47:23.380 --> 00:47:26.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: pursuing investment-led growth.

asr-000351
00:47:26.380 --> 00:47:27.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: For the Philippines,

asr-000352
00:47:27.380 --> 00:47:31.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the wider deficit primarily reflects strong demand

asr-000353
00:47:31.380 --> 00:47:34.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: for capital goods and other productive imports

asr-000354
00:47:34.380 --> 00:47:37.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: needed to support infrastructure development

asr-000355
00:47:37.380 --> 00:47:40.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and expand productive activity.

asr-000356
00:47:40.380 --> 00:47:45.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: How is this deficit being supported right now?

asr-000357
00:47:45.380 --> 00:47:47.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This highlights the importance

asr-000358
00:47:47.380 --> 00:47:50.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: of structural foreign exchange inflows,

asr-000359
00:47:50.380 --> 00:47:53.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the remittances, the revenues from BPO's,

asr-000360
00:47:53.380 --> 00:47:58.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and also the inflows from foreign direct investments.

asr-000361
00:47:58.380 --> 00:48:03.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: We are also maintaining enough buffers

asr-000362
00:48:03.380 --> 00:48:05.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: in terms of international reserves.

asr-000363
00:48:05.380 --> 00:48:08.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: As of now, our international reserve stands

asr-000364
00:48:08.380 --> 00:48:10.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: at almost $105 billion.

asr-000365
00:48:10.380 --> 00:48:15.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: That is as of end June 2026,

asr-000366
00:48:15.380 --> 00:48:18.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and it's equivalent to about seven months' worth

asr-000367
00:48:18.380 --> 00:48:22.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: of imports of goods and services.

asr-000368
00:48:22.380 --> 00:48:27.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: So this is the general macroeconomic landscape

asr-000369
00:48:27.380 --> 00:48:31.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: that we are working with at this time.

asr-000370
00:48:31.380 --> 00:48:35.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And the key assumptions behind the proposed national budget

asr-000371
00:48:35.380 --> 00:48:38.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: for fiscal year 2027

asr-000372
00:48:38.380 --> 00:48:40.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: are shown in this particular slide.

asr-000373
00:48:40.380 --> 00:48:43.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: In terms of inflation,

asr-000374
00:48:43.380 --> 00:48:44.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: as mentioned earlier,

asr-000375
00:48:44.380 --> 00:48:46.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: our latest inflation forecast

asr-000376
00:48:46.380 --> 00:48:51.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: points to still elevated inflation for 2026

asr-000377
00:48:51.380 --> 00:48:54.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: before easing in 2027.

asr-000378
00:48:54.380 --> 00:48:57.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: For the national government budget purposes,

asr-000379
00:48:57.380 --> 00:48:59.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: we assume that headline inflation

asr-000380
00:48:59.380 --> 00:49:04.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to be around 4% to 5% for 2027.

asr-000381
00:49:04.380 --> 00:49:09.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Oil prices remain volatile and highly uncertain,

asr-000382
00:49:09.380 --> 00:49:12.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: largely dependent on geopolitical developments,

asr-000383
00:49:12.380 --> 00:49:14.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: particularly in the Middle East.

asr-000384
00:49:14.380 --> 00:49:17.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Markets right now are pointing to some decline

asr-000385
00:49:17.380 --> 00:49:20.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: in the price of Dubai crude oil

asr-000386
00:49:20.380 --> 00:49:24.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to about the range of $70 to $90 per barrel

asr-000387
00:49:24.380 --> 00:49:28.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: on average in 2027.

asr-000388
00:49:28.380 --> 00:49:31.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Exchange rate will be broadly stable

asr-000389
00:49:31.380 --> 00:49:32.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: against the US dollar,

asr-000390
00:49:32.380 --> 00:49:34.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: reflecting external developments

asr-000391
00:49:34.380 --> 00:49:38.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and also at the same time some domestic headwinds.

asr-000392
00:49:38.380 --> 00:49:40.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: On the interest rates,

asr-000393
00:49:40.380 --> 00:49:42.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: particularly domestic interest rates,

asr-000394
00:49:42.380 --> 00:49:46.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the one-year T-bill rate will range around 5% to 6%

asr-000395
00:49:46.380 --> 00:49:49.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: in 2026 and 2027,

asr-000396
00:49:49.380 --> 00:49:53.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and this reflects the country's fiscal condition

asr-000397
00:49:53.380 --> 00:49:56.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and the policy of continued consolidation.

asr-000398
00:49:56.380 --> 00:49:59.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: In the international interest rates,

asr-000399
00:49:59.380 --> 00:50:03.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the six-month secured overnight financing rate,

asr-000400
00:50:03.380 --> 00:50:07.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: which is the global short-term rate benchmark in US dollars,

asr-000401
00:50:07.380 --> 00:50:15.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: is assumed to be within 3% to 4% in 2026 as well as in 2027.

asr-000402
00:50:15.380 --> 00:50:18.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This reflects expectations that the US Fed

asr-000403
00:50:18.380 --> 00:50:21.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: may maintain a relatively cautious stance

asr-000404
00:50:21.380 --> 00:50:24.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: in terms of monetary policy.

asr-000405
00:50:24.380 --> 00:50:27.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Finally, our exports of goods will grow modestly,

asr-000406
00:50:27.380 --> 00:50:33.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: boosted by firm global demand for electronics and manufactures,

asr-000407
00:50:33.380 --> 00:50:36.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: but constrained by the slow global economy

asr-000408
00:50:36.380 --> 00:50:40.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and increased global trade uncertainty.

asr-000409
00:50:40.380 --> 00:50:43.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Let me end with some remarks.

asr-000410
00:50:43.380 --> 00:50:47.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: First, inflation outlook remains elevated,

asr-000411
00:50:47.380 --> 00:50:52.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: requiring measured action to anchor inflation expectations

asr-000412
00:50:52.380 --> 00:50:56.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and contain broadening price pressures.

asr-000413
00:50:56.380 --> 00:50:59.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: We have adequate external buffers

asr-000414
00:50:59.380 --> 00:51:02.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and a resilient, healthy banking system

asr-000415
00:51:02.380 --> 00:51:06.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to provide support to domestic economic activity.

asr-000416
00:51:06.380 --> 00:51:07.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Moving forward,

asr-000417
00:51:07.380 --> 00:51:11.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the BSP is prepared to take further monetary actions

asr-000418
00:51:11.380 --> 00:51:14.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: if needed to ensure its primary mandate

asr-000419
00:51:14.380 --> 00:51:17.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: of maintaining price stability

asr-000420
00:51:17.380 --> 00:51:21.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: conducive to sustainable and durable growth.

asr-000421
00:51:21.380 --> 00:51:24.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: We end here, Madam Chair.

asr-000422
00:51:24.380 --> 00:51:27.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Again, thank you very much.

asr-000423
00:51:27.380 --> 00:51:30.380
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you very much to the BSP family.

asr-000424
00:51:30.380 --> 00:51:34.380
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you to Governor Eli Remolona Jr.

asr-000425
00:51:34.380 --> 00:51:36.380
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: and Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald,

asr-000426
00:51:36.380 --> 00:51:37.380
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: and Deputy Governor Abenoja.

asr-000427
00:51:37.380 --> 00:51:38.380
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you very much.

asr-000428
00:51:38.380 --> 00:51:40.380
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Next, we move to the presentation

asr-000429
00:51:40.380 --> 00:51:43.380
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: of the Department of Economy, Planning and Development,

asr-000430
00:51:43.380 --> 00:51:44.380
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: or DEPDev,

asr-000431
00:51:44.380 --> 00:51:47.380
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: headed by Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan.

asr-000432
00:51:47.380 --> 00:51:52.380
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Secretary Balisacan, kindly proceed po.

asr-000433
00:51:52.380 --> 00:51:53.380
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you very much.

asr-000434
00:51:53.380 --> 00:51:57.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Thank you, Speaker Di III,

asr-000435
00:51:57.380 --> 00:51:59.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Chairperson Swan Singh,

asr-000436
00:51:59.380 --> 00:52:03.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and distinguished members of the Committee on Appropriations

asr-000437
00:52:03.380 --> 00:52:04.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: for this opportunity

asr-000438
00:52:04.380 --> 00:52:06.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: to discuss the state of the Philippine economy

asr-000439
00:52:06.380 --> 00:52:11.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and our economic directions moving forward.

asr-000440
00:52:11.380 --> 00:52:13.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: My task this morning

asr-000441
00:52:13.380 --> 00:52:16.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: is to provide the economic development context

asr-000442
00:52:16.380 --> 00:52:19.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: for the proposed 2027 National Budget,

asr-000443
00:52:19.380 --> 00:52:22.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: where the economy stands,

asr-000444
00:52:22.380 --> 00:52:25.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: why growth has slowed sharply in recent quarters,

asr-000445
00:52:25.380 --> 00:52:27.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and what directions must guide

asr-000446
00:52:27.380 --> 00:52:32.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: our policies and investments moving forward.

asr-000447
00:52:32.380 --> 00:52:35.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The 2027 budget must help us

asr-000448
00:52:35.380 --> 00:52:38.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: protect the gains already achieved,

asr-000449
00:52:38.380 --> 00:52:40.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: address critical implementations

asr-000450
00:52:40.380 --> 00:52:42.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and structural bottlenecks,

asr-000451
00:52:42.380 --> 00:52:45.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and restore the economy to a faster,

asr-000452
00:52:45.380 --> 00:52:49.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: more durable, and inclusive growth path.

asr-000453
00:52:49.380 --> 00:52:52.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I will cover three areas.

asr-000454
00:52:52.380 --> 00:52:54.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: First, our economic performance

asr-000455
00:52:54.380 --> 00:52:56.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and recent developments.

asr-000456
00:52:56.380 --> 00:52:58.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Second, the emerging risk

asr-000457
00:52:58.380 --> 00:53:01.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and persistent structural constraints.

asr-000458
00:53:01.380 --> 00:53:04.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And third, our outlook and priorities

asr-000459
00:53:04.380 --> 00:53:06.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: for recovering growth

asr-000460
00:53:06.380 --> 00:53:10.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and laying the foundations for sustained development.

asr-000461
00:53:10.380 --> 00:53:14.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Let me begin with our economic performance.

asr-000462
00:53:14.380 --> 00:53:17.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Over the past several years,

asr-000463
00:53:17.380 --> 00:53:21.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the Philippine economy achieved important gains

asr-000464
00:53:21.380 --> 00:53:26.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: in growth, employment, and poverty reduction.

asr-000465
00:53:26.380 --> 00:53:28.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: More recent developments, however,

asr-000466
00:53:28.380 --> 00:53:32.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: show a sharp loss of momentum.

asr-000467
00:53:32.380 --> 00:53:34.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Taking the longer view,

asr-000468
00:53:34.380 --> 00:53:37.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the Philippine economy has become stronger.

asr-000469
00:53:37.380 --> 00:53:40.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: From 2010 to 2025,

asr-000470
00:53:40.380 --> 00:53:45.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: real GDP grew by an average of 5.1% a year,

asr-000471
00:53:45.380 --> 00:53:48.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: faster than the 4.2% average

asr-000472
00:53:48.380 --> 00:53:52.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: recorded during the preceding 15 years.

asr-000473
00:53:52.380 --> 00:53:56.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Following the pandemic,

asr-000474
00:53:56.380 --> 00:53:59.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: economic growth averaged 5.8%

asr-000475
00:53:59.380 --> 00:54:02.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: from 2022 to 2025.

asr-000476
00:54:02.380 --> 00:54:06.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: However, momentum weakened sharply

asr-000477
00:54:06.380 --> 00:54:09.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: beginning in the second half of 2025,

asr-000478
00:54:09.380 --> 00:54:12.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: with growth slowing further to 2.6%

asr-000479
00:54:12.380 --> 00:54:14.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: in the first half of this year.

asr-000480
00:54:14.380 --> 00:54:19.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This sharp deceleration defines our immediate challenge

asr-000481
00:54:19.380 --> 00:54:22.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: to recover growth without losing

asr-000482
00:54:22.380 --> 00:54:25.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the important development gains already achieved.

asr-000483
00:54:25.380 --> 00:54:29.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: That milestone is the Philippines' transition

asr-000484
00:54:29.380 --> 00:54:31.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: to upper middle-income status

asr-000485
00:54:31.380 --> 00:54:34.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: after nearly four decades

asr-000486
00:54:34.380 --> 00:54:37.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: as a lower middle-income economy.

asr-000487
00:54:37.380 --> 00:54:41.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The country's gross national income per capita,

asr-000488
00:54:41.380 --> 00:54:42.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: or GNI,

asr-000489
00:54:42.380 --> 00:54:47.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: reached US$4,850 in 2025,

asr-000490
00:54:47.380 --> 00:54:49.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: surpassing the World Bank's threshold

asr-000491
00:54:49.380 --> 00:54:53.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: of US$4,636.

asr-000492
00:54:53.380 --> 00:54:56.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: As the chart on the right shows,

asr-000493
00:54:56.380 --> 00:54:59.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the Philippines has also moved closer

asr-000494
00:54:59.380 --> 00:55:00.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: to its Asian peers,

asr-000495
00:55:00.380 --> 00:55:04.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: although considerable income gaps remain.

asr-000496
00:55:04.380 --> 00:55:07.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Reaching upper middle-income status

asr-000497
00:55:07.380 --> 00:55:09.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: is an important achievement,

asr-000498
00:55:09.380 --> 00:55:13.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: but it is or it is not an end in itself.

asr-000499
00:55:13.380 --> 00:55:17.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The greater challenge is to translate this progress

asr-000500
00:55:17.380 --> 00:55:20.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: into better jobs, higher incomes,

asr-000501
00:55:20.380 --> 00:55:23.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and improved living standards for Filipinos.

asr-000502
00:55:23.380 --> 00:55:27.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: To do so, we must first understand the factors

asr-000503
00:55:27.380 --> 00:55:29.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: behind the recent loss of economic momentum.

asr-000504
00:55:30.380 --> 00:55:35.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The sharp slowdown largely reflected

asr-000505
00:55:35.380 --> 00:55:37.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: weaker domestic demand,

asr-000506
00:55:37.380 --> 00:55:40.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: as governance and corruption concerns

asr-000507
00:55:40.380 --> 00:55:43.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and the Middle East conflict weighed

asr-000508
00:55:43.380 --> 00:55:46.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: on consumer and business confidence.

asr-000509
00:55:46.380 --> 00:55:49.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Domestic demand grew by only 1.5%

asr-000510
00:55:49.380 --> 00:55:51.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: in the first half of 2026,

asr-000511
00:55:51.380 --> 00:55:56.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: down from 5.7% in the same period last year.

asr-000512
00:55:56.380 --> 00:55:59.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Investment contracted by 6.5%,

asr-000513
00:55:59.380 --> 00:56:02.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: driven largely by the sharp decline

asr-000514
00:56:02.380 --> 00:56:04.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: in public construction.

asr-000515
00:56:04.380 --> 00:56:08.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Household consumption growth also eased to 2.9%,

asr-000516
00:56:08.380 --> 00:56:13.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: amid elevated inflation and weaker confidence.

asr-000517
00:56:13.380 --> 00:56:16.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Exports provided some support,

asr-000518
00:56:16.380 --> 00:56:18.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: growing by 10%.

asr-000519
00:56:18.380 --> 00:56:21.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: On the production side, however,

asr-000520
00:56:21.380 --> 00:56:24.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: services remained the principal source of growth,

asr-000521
00:56:24.380 --> 00:56:28.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: while industry contracted and agriculture

asr-000522
00:56:28.380 --> 00:56:31.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: made only a modest contribution.

asr-000523
00:56:31.380 --> 00:56:34.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The weakening of economic activity

asr-000524
00:56:34.380 --> 00:56:37.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: has also begun to affect the labour market.

asr-000525
00:56:37.380 --> 00:56:42.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The post-pandemic expansion generated 4 million net jobs

asr-000526
00:56:42.380 --> 00:56:47.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: between the first half of 2022 and the first half of 2026,

asr-000527
00:56:47.380 --> 00:56:51.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: demonstrating how economic growth can create opportunities

asr-000528
00:56:51.380 --> 00:56:54.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and improve livelihoods.

asr-000529
00:56:54.380 --> 00:56:57.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: However, as growth slowed,

asr-000530
00:56:57.380 --> 00:57:03.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: total employment declined by 166,000 in the past year.

asr-000531
00:57:03.380 --> 00:57:08.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The unemployment rate also rose to 4.2% in June 2026,

asr-000532
00:57:08.380 --> 00:57:11.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: from 3.1% a year earlier.

asr-000533
00:57:11.380 --> 00:57:15.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: These recent developments underscore the urgency

asr-000534
00:57:15.380 --> 00:57:17.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: of restoring economic momentum

asr-000535
00:57:17.380 --> 00:57:22.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and generating more and better quality jobs.

asr-000536
00:57:22.380 --> 00:57:26.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The benefits of recent economic growth extended beyond employment,

asr-000537
00:57:26.380 --> 00:57:29.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: poverty declined substantially,

asr-000538
00:57:29.380 --> 00:57:33.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: regardless of the poverty threshold or norm used.

asr-000539
00:57:33.380 --> 00:57:37.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Based on the country's official poverty lines

asr-000540
00:57:37.380 --> 00:57:40.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and the preliminary estimates for 2025,

asr-000541
00:57:40.380 --> 00:57:42.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: poverty incidence,

asr-000542
00:57:42.380 --> 00:57:46.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: or the proportion of the population deemed poor among Filipinos,

asr-000543
00:57:46.380 --> 00:57:54.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: fell from 18.1% in 2021 to 9.7% in 2025.

asr-000544
00:57:54.380 --> 00:57:58.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This means that 8.8 million Filipinos

asr-000545
00:57:58.380 --> 00:58:01.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: were lifted out of poverty over this period.

asr-000546
00:58:01.380 --> 00:58:07.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: These gains reflect not only the recovery of incomes and employment,

asr-000547
00:58:07.380 --> 00:58:11.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: but also the sustained implementation of social protection programs.

asr-000548
00:58:11.380 --> 00:58:16.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: However, these hard-won gains remain vulnerable,

asr-000549
00:58:16.380 --> 00:58:19.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: particularly to high inflation,

asr-000550
00:58:19.380 --> 00:58:23.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: which disproportionately affects poor and low-income households.

asr-000551
00:58:24.380 --> 00:58:27.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: As Governor Remolona just mentioned,

asr-000552
00:58:27.380 --> 00:58:29.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: or discussed earlier,

asr-000553
00:58:29.380 --> 00:58:32.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: inflation rose sharply beginning in March,

asr-000554
00:58:32.380 --> 00:58:35.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: driven largely by the effects of the Middle East conflict

asr-000555
00:58:35.380 --> 00:58:39.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: on global oil and commodity prices.

asr-000556
00:58:39.380 --> 00:58:43.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Headline inflation is slightly to 6.2% in July

asr-000557
00:58:43.380 --> 00:58:47.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: from 6.4% in June,

asr-000558
00:58:47.380 --> 00:58:53.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: but it remains well above the government's target range.

asr-000559
00:58:53.380 --> 00:58:57.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: High inflation erodes household purchasing power,

asr-000560
00:58:57.380 --> 00:59:01.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: disproportionately affecting poor and low-income families.

asr-000561
00:59:01.380 --> 00:59:03.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The burden is even heavier

asr-000562
00:59:03.380 --> 00:59:08.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: when food prices rise faster than non-food prices,

asr-000563
00:59:08.380 --> 00:59:13.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: as food accounts for a much larger share of total consumption spending

asr-000564
00:59:13.380 --> 00:59:18.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: among low-income families than among high-income families.

asr-000565
00:59:18.380 --> 00:59:20.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: If inflation remains elevated,

asr-000566
00:59:20.380 --> 00:59:22.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: it could slow or even reverse

asr-000567
00:59:22.380 --> 00:59:25.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: our recent gains in poverty reduction.

asr-000568
00:59:25.380 --> 00:59:28.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Protecting these gains while recovering economic growth

asr-000569
00:59:28.380 --> 00:59:32.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: will require us to address both emerging risk

asr-000570
00:59:32.380 --> 00:59:36.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and the economy's persistent structural constraints.

asr-000571
00:59:36.380 --> 00:59:42.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Beyond the immediate concerns of slower growth and elevated inflation,

asr-000572
00:59:42.380 --> 00:59:45.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: persistent structural constraints continue to limit

asr-000573
00:59:45.380 --> 00:59:49.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the economy's productive capacity and resilience.

asr-000574
00:59:49.380 --> 00:59:51.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Let me now turn to these constraints.

asr-000575
00:59:52.380 --> 00:59:55.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: A central structural challenge

asr-000576
00:59:55.380 --> 00:59:58.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: is the economy's heavy reliance on household consumption

asr-000577
00:59:58.380 --> 01:00:00.000
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: under the

asr-000578
01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:06.660
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: side and services on the production side of the economy. Consumption remains the

asr-000579
01:00:06.660 --> 01:00:11.520
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: principal driver of economic growth, while the contributions of fixed

asr-000580
01:00:11.520 --> 01:00:18.840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: investment exports, net of imports, have been relatively limited. Similarly,

asr-000581
01:00:18.840 --> 01:00:24.120
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: services account for most of the expansion, while agriculture and industry

asr-000582
01:00:24.120 --> 01:00:31.360
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: have contributed much less. The experience of successful economies shows

asr-000583
01:00:31.360 --> 01:00:35.540
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: that sustained progress requires mobilizing other sources of growth,

asr-000584
01:00:35.540 --> 01:00:43.300
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: notably investment, exports, agriculture, and industry. We must therefore broaden

asr-000585
01:00:43.300 --> 01:00:47.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the source of growth by strengthening investment and exports, while

asr-000586
01:00:47.380 --> 01:00:54.100
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: revitalizing agriculture and industry. The urgency of this task is evident

asr-000587
01:00:54.100 --> 01:01:02.480
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: from our performance relative to our ASEAN peers. As the charts show, the

asr-000588
01:01:02.480 --> 01:01:07.700
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Philippines continues to trail several neighboring economies in both

asr-000589
01:01:07.700 --> 01:01:14.020
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: fixed investment and exports, despite improvements in recent years.

asr-000590
01:01:14.020 --> 01:01:19.480
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Investment expands productive capacity, facilitates the adoption of new

asr-000591
01:01:19.480 --> 01:01:24.060
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: technologies, and creates better jobs.

asr-000592
01:01:24.100 --> 01:01:29.280
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Exports enable domestic firms to reach larger markets, achieve economies of

asr-000593
01:01:29.280 --> 01:01:35.160
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: scale, and become more competitive. Mobilizing greater investment and

asr-000594
01:01:35.160 --> 01:01:40.700
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: improving export competitiveness will depend, critically, on high quality and

asr-000595
01:01:40.700 --> 01:01:46.620
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: reliable infrastructure. The government has substantially increased

asr-000596
01:01:46.620 --> 01:01:53.280
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: infrastructure spending in recent years. Yet, this higher level of expenditure has

asr-000597
01:01:53.280 --> 01:01:54.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: not translated for the better. The government has substantially increased infrastructure spending in recent years. Yet, this higher level of expenditure has not translated

asr-000598
01:01:54.080 --> 01:01:59.340
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: fully into stronger infrastructure competitiveness and the Philippines continues to trail several ASEAN peers.

asr-000599
01:01:59.340 --> 01:02:02.940
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: fully into stronger infrastructure competitiveness and the Philippines continues to trail several ASEAN peers.

asr-000600
01:02:02.940 --> 01:02:09.720
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This gap shows that the level of spending alone is not enough. We must also

asr-000601
01:02:09.720 --> 01:02:15.280
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: improve project selection, appraisal, procurement, implementation, and

asr-000602
01:02:15.280 --> 01:02:19.420
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: maintenance to ensure that public resources deliver high-quality

asr-000603
01:02:19.420 --> 01:02:23.760
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: infrastructure on time and at reasonable cost.

asr-000604
01:02:24.080 --> 01:02:39.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Closing our infrastructure gaps will reduce production and logistic costs, connect people and markets, crowd in private investment, and strengthen the country's competitiveness.

asr-000605
01:02:39.080 --> 01:02:48.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Beyond physical infrastructure, faster growth also requires greater innovation and stronger productivity.

asr-000606
01:02:48.080 --> 01:02:59.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The Philippines has made encouraging progress in innovation, as reflected in its improved ranking in the Global Innovation Index.

asr-000607
01:02:59.080 --> 01:03:15.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: However, these gains have yet to translate into stronger overall productivity, that is, how efficiently the economy combines its workers, capital, technology, and other resources to produce goods and services.

asr-000608
01:03:15.080 --> 01:03:18.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: As the chart on the right shows,

asr-000609
01:03:18.080 --> 01:03:25.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: our productivity performance remains weak relative to several of our regional peers.

asr-000610
01:03:25.080 --> 01:03:34.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Innovation contributes to development only when new knowledge and technologies are widely adapted by firms, farms, and workers,

asr-000611
01:03:34.080 --> 01:03:42.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and translated into more efficient production, better products, and higher value activities.

asr-000612
01:03:42.080 --> 01:03:48.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We must therefore strengthen the links among research, skills development, technology adoption,

asr-000613
01:03:48.080 --> 01:03:52.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: commercialization, and production.

asr-000614
01:03:52.080 --> 01:03:57.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The weaknesses we have discussed do not arise from a single source.

asr-000615
01:03:57.080 --> 01:04:04.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: They reflect persistent and interconnected constraints across markets and institutions.

asr-000616
01:04:04.080 --> 01:04:12.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: These include infrastructure and human capital gaps, regulatory and administrative burdens, limited access to finance and technology,

asr-000617
01:04:12.080 --> 01:04:17.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: weak competition in key sectors, and continuing governance concerns.

asr-000618
01:04:18.080 --> 01:04:25.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Together, these constraints raise the cost of doing business, discourage investment and innovation,

asr-000619
01:04:25.080 --> 01:04:33.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and limit the ability of firms and workers to move into more productive and higher-value activities.

asr-000620
01:04:33.080 --> 01:04:45.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Addressing them requires coordinated action across government in close partnership with Congress, the private sector, and other stakeholders.

asr-000621
01:04:45.080 --> 01:04:47.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Having identified these challenges,

asr-000622
01:04:47.080 --> 01:04:54.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I now turn to our growth targets and the priorities for moving the economy forward.

asr-000623
01:04:54.080 --> 01:05:00.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Our directions remain anchored in the Philippine Development Plan.

asr-000624
01:05:00.080 --> 01:05:06.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Over the Administration's final two years, the emphasis is on accelerating execution,

asr-000625
01:05:06.080 --> 01:05:14.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: resolving implementation bottlenecks, and translating reforms into concrete results.

asr-000626
01:05:14.080 --> 01:05:16.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Given the sharp slowdown in recent years,

asr-000627
01:05:16.080 --> 01:05:25.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: economic growth is projected at 3.5 to 4.5 percent in 2025.

asr-000628
01:05:25.080 --> 01:05:31.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: With faster implementation of public programs and infrastructure projects,

asr-000629
01:05:31.080 --> 01:05:34.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: improved domestic supply conditions,

asr-000630
01:05:34.080 --> 01:05:37.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and restored consumer and investor confidence,

asr-000631
01:05:37.080 --> 01:05:43.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: growth is expected to recover to 5 to 6 percent in the next two years.

asr-000632
01:05:43.080 --> 01:05:45.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Inflation is expected to recover to 5 to 6 percent in the next two years.

asr-000633
01:05:45.080 --> 01:05:51.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Inflation is expected to remain elevated in 2026, as shown earlier by BSP,

asr-000634
01:05:51.080 --> 01:05:54.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: eased to 4 to 5 percent in 2027,

asr-000635
01:05:54.080 --> 01:06:02.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and returned to the government's targets of 2 to 4 percent target range by 2028.

asr-000636
01:06:02.080 --> 01:06:08.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Meanwhile, employment conditions are expected to improve as economic growth recovers,

asr-000637
01:06:08.080 --> 01:06:12.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: keeping unemployment within the government's target range.

asr-000638
01:06:12.080 --> 01:06:19.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Achieving these outcomes will require disciplined and coordinated execution across government,

asr-000639
01:06:19.080 --> 01:06:24.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: along with the timely implementation of reforms that encourage private investment

asr-000640
01:06:24.080 --> 01:06:27.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and expand the economy's productive capacity.

asr-000641
01:06:27.080 --> 01:06:30.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: These targets are attainable,

asr-000642
01:06:30.080 --> 01:06:36.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: but they remain subject to significant domestic and external risk.

asr-000643
01:06:36.080 --> 01:06:40.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Achieving our growth, inflation, and employment targets

asr-000644
01:06:40.080 --> 01:06:45.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: will require us to manage significant domestic and external risk.

asr-000645
01:06:45.080 --> 01:06:51.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Foremost among the domestic risks are further delays in the execution of public investments,

asr-000646
01:06:51.080 --> 01:06:53.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: resulting in continued underspending,

asr-000647
01:06:53.080 --> 01:06:56.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: as well as continuing governance concerns

asr-000648
01:06:56.080 --> 01:07:01.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: that could further weaken consumer and investor confidence.

asr-000649
01:07:01.080 --> 01:07:05.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Severe weather disturbances could also constrain food production

asr-000650
01:07:05.080 --> 01:07:09.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and intensify inflationary pressures.

asr-000651
01:07:10.080 --> 01:07:13.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Externally, the prolonged Middle East conflict

asr-000652
01:07:13.080 --> 01:07:17.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: could keep global oil and commodity prices elevated,

asr-000653
01:07:17.080 --> 01:07:21.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: while geopolitical and trade tensions may weaken global demand

asr-000654
01:07:21.080 --> 01:07:25.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and disrupt supply chains.

asr-000655
01:07:25.080 --> 01:07:31.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: These risks reinforce the need for timely and coordinated policies and execution

asr-000656
01:07:31.080 --> 01:07:38.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: that address immediate pressures while strengthening the economy's productive capacity.

asr-000657
01:07:38.080 --> 01:07:39.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: In the near term,

asr-000658
01:07:39.080 --> 01:07:44.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: our priorities are to protect vulnerable households,

asr-000659
01:07:44.080 --> 01:07:46.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: accelerate public investments,

asr-000660
01:07:46.080 --> 01:07:48.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and restore confidence.

asr-000661
01:07:48.080 --> 01:07:51.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: First, we will caution poor and low-income families

asr-000662
01:07:51.080 --> 01:07:55.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: from elevated food prices and supply disruptions

asr-000663
01:07:55.080 --> 01:07:58.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: through targeted and timely assistance,

asr-000664
01:07:58.080 --> 01:08:03.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: while strengthening domestic food supply and maintaining adequate buffers.

asr-000665
01:08:03.080 --> 01:08:09.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Second, implementing agencies will accelerate high-impact infrastructure projects

asr-000666
01:08:09.080 --> 01:08:15.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: through catch-up plans with clear milestones and accountability measures.

asr-000667
01:08:15.080 --> 01:08:18.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This is essential to reverse underspending

asr-000668
01:08:18.080 --> 01:08:22.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and restore public investment as a driver of growth.

asr-000669
01:08:22.080 --> 01:08:26.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Third, we need to address governance and corruption concerns

asr-000670
01:08:26.080 --> 01:08:29.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: by strengthening transparency and accountability,

asr-000671
01:08:29.080 --> 01:08:31.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: improving monitoring,

asr-000672
01:08:31.080 --> 01:08:35.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and ensuring the efficient use of public resources.

asr-000673
01:08:35.080 --> 01:08:38.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: These measures are critical to rebuilding consumer,

asr-000674
01:08:38.080 --> 01:08:43.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: business, and investor confidence.

asr-000675
01:08:43.080 --> 01:08:44.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Alongside these measures,

asr-000676
01:08:44.080 --> 01:08:46.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: our immediate interventions,

asr-000677
01:08:46.080 --> 01:08:50.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: we must sustain investments that expand the economy's productive capacity

asr-000678
01:08:50.080 --> 01:08:54.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: over the short to medium term.

asr-000679
01:08:54.080 --> 01:08:55.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Over the short to medium term,

asr-000680
01:08:55.080 --> 01:09:00.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: limited public resources must be directed toward high-impact,

asr-000681
01:09:00.080 --> 01:09:03.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: implementation-ready investments.

asr-000682
01:09:03.080 --> 01:09:07.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Priorities include addressing learning poverty and classroom shortages,

asr-000683
01:09:07.080 --> 01:09:10.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: equipping workers with future-ready skills,

asr-000684
01:09:10.080 --> 01:09:13.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: strengthening primary health care,

asr-000685
01:09:13.080 --> 01:09:16.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: particularly in underserved areas,

asr-000686
01:09:16.080 --> 01:09:20.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: raising farm productivity through climate-resilient technologies

asr-000687
01:09:20.080 --> 01:09:23.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and better post-harvest infrastructure,

asr-000688
01:09:23.080 --> 01:09:27.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and accelerating transport, logistics, energy,

asr-000689
01:09:27.080 --> 01:09:29.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and digital infrastructure

asr-000690
01:09:29.080 --> 01:09:34.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: through the Build Better More program and public-private partnerships.

asr-000691
01:09:34.080 --> 01:09:36.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: These investments must be pursued

asr-000692
01:09:36.080 --> 01:09:40.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: while safeguarding fiscal sustainability.

asr-000693
01:09:40.080 --> 01:09:43.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This requires stronger coordination of planning,

asr-000694
01:09:43.080 --> 01:09:45.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: investment programming,

asr-000695
01:09:45.080 --> 01:09:49.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: budgeting, and execution of infrastructure and social programs,

asr-000696
01:09:49.080 --> 01:09:51.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: improved spending efficiency,

asr-000697
01:09:51.080 --> 01:09:55.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: modernized tax and customs administration,

asr-000698
01:09:55.080 --> 01:10:02.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and revenue measures that do not erode the government's fiscal position.

asr-000699
01:10:02.080 --> 01:10:05.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Beyond addressing immediate challenges,

asr-000700
01:10:05.080 --> 01:10:09.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: sustained and structural reforms will be needed to raise productivity,

asr-000701
01:10:09.080 --> 01:10:11.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: strengthen competitiveness,

asr-000702
01:10:11.080 --> 01:10:15.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and expand the economy's long-term growth potential.

asr-000703
01:10:15.080 --> 01:10:20.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Key priorities include ensuring more reliable and affordable energy

asr-000704
01:10:20.080 --> 01:10:22.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: by expanding renewable generation,

asr-000705
01:10:22.080 --> 01:10:25.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: modernizing the power grid,

asr-000706
01:10:25.080 --> 01:10:28.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: streamlining net metering and permitting processes,

asr-000707
01:10:28.080 --> 01:10:33.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and strengthening competition in the electricity market.

asr-000708
01:10:33.080 --> 01:10:34.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Domestic production

asr-000709
01:10:34.080 --> 01:10:38.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and external competitiveness must likewise be strengthened

asr-000710
01:10:38.080 --> 01:10:42.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: by moving into higher value segments of global value chains,

asr-000711
01:10:42.080 --> 01:10:47.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: fostering stronger linkages between multinational and domestic firms,

asr-000712
01:10:47.080 --> 01:10:51.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: sustaining the country's advantage in high-value services,

asr-000713
01:10:51.080 --> 01:10:55.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and expanding market access for Philippine exports.

asr-000714
01:10:55.080 --> 01:10:59.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Deeper financial and capital markets will also be essential

asr-000715
01:10:59.080 --> 01:11:02.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: to mobilize long-term financing for infrastructure

asr-000716
01:11:02.080 --> 01:11:04.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and productive enterprises.

asr-000717
01:11:04.080 --> 01:11:11.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Legislation will be indispensable to advancing this reform agenda.

asr-000718
01:11:11.080 --> 01:11:16.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The priority measures span four broad areas.

asr-000719
01:11:16.080 --> 01:11:22.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Governance and anti-corruption reforms include measures on political dynasties,

asr-000720
01:11:22.080 --> 01:11:24.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the party-less system,

asr-000721
01:11:24.080 --> 01:11:26.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: freedom of information,

asr-000722
01:11:26.080 --> 01:11:28.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: bank secrecy law,

asr-000723
01:11:28.080 --> 01:11:30.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and public spending or budgeting.

asr-000724
01:11:30.080 --> 01:11:33.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Economic growth and resilience measures

asr-000725
01:11:33.080 --> 01:11:40.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: cover tax reforms and amendments affecting the coconut and fisheries sectors.

asr-000726
01:11:40.080 --> 01:11:43.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Energy priorities include amendments to EPIRA

asr-000727
01:11:43.080 --> 01:11:48.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and legislation on waste to energy.

asr-000728
01:11:48.080 --> 01:11:51.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Measures on education, health, and social protection

asr-000729
01:11:51.080 --> 01:11:55.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: seek to improve nutrition, accelerate classroom production,

asr-000730
01:11:55.080 --> 01:11:57.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: expand access to education,

asr-000731
01:11:57.080 --> 01:12:01.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and strengthen assistance for vulnerable Filipinos.

asr-000732
01:12:01.080 --> 01:12:07.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Congress' continued partnership will be critical to advancing these reforms,

asr-000733
01:12:07.080 --> 01:12:11.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: sustaining growth, and improving Filipino lives.

asr-000734
01:12:11.080 --> 01:12:16.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: As we enter the final years of the administration,

asr-000735
01:12:16.080 --> 01:12:20.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the objective is to turn reforms into results.

asr-000736
01:12:20.080 --> 01:12:22.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We will consolidate our gains,

asr-000737
01:12:22.080 --> 01:12:25.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: address critical implementation bottlenecks,

asr-000738
01:12:25.080 --> 01:12:28.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and advance strategic measures

asr-000739
01:12:28.080 --> 01:12:30.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: to deliver people-centered growth

asr-000740
01:12:30.080 --> 01:12:33.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and a more inclusive and resilient future.

asr-000741
01:12:33.080 --> 01:12:34.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Thank you.

asr-000742
01:12:38.080 --> 01:12:41.080
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you very much, Secretary Balisacan.

asr-000743
01:12:41.080 --> 01:12:45.080
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We'll now move to the presentation from the Department of Finance.

asr-000744
01:12:45.080 --> 01:12:49.080
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: May I now recognize the Honorable Secretary Frederick Go

asr-000745
01:12:49.080 --> 01:12:51.080
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: for the presentation of the DOF family.

asr-000746
01:12:52.080 --> 01:12:53.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Good morning.

asr-000747
01:12:53.080 --> 01:12:56.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The honorable speaker, Bodjie Dy III,

asr-000748
01:12:56.080 --> 01:12:58.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Chair Mika Suansing,

asr-000749
01:12:58.080 --> 01:13:00.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Senior Vice Chair Abed Garcia,

asr-000750
01:13:00.080 --> 01:13:03.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Majority Floor Leader Marcos,

asr-000751
01:13:03.080 --> 01:13:06.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: all the honorable members of this committee,

asr-000752
01:13:06.080 --> 01:13:10.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: thank you for this opportunity to brief the House of Representatives

asr-000753
01:13:10.080 --> 01:13:14.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: on the national government's fiscal position.

asr-000754
01:13:14.080 --> 01:13:19.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Our fiscal position today has been shaped by key economic developments,

asr-000755
01:13:19.080 --> 01:13:23.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from the circumstances this administration inherited

asr-000756
01:13:23.080 --> 01:13:28.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to the global conditions that have influenced our fiscal path since then.

asr-000757
01:13:28.080 --> 01:13:30.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Allow me to discuss briefly,

asr-000758
01:13:30.080 --> 01:13:33.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to provide context to where we are today

asr-000759
01:13:33.080 --> 01:13:35.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and where we are headed.

asr-000760
01:13:36.080 --> 01:13:41.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: When the Marcos Jr. administration assumed office in 2022,

asr-000761
01:13:41.080 --> 01:13:47.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: it inherited a massive 12.79 trillion debt,

asr-000762
01:13:47.080 --> 01:13:51.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the bulk of which was incurred from pandemic spending.

asr-000763
01:13:51.080 --> 01:13:54.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So when the economy began to recover,

asr-000764
01:13:54.080 --> 01:13:57.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the challenge before the administration was clear.

asr-000765
01:13:57.080 --> 01:13:59.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: To rebuild fiscal space,

asr-000766
01:13:59.080 --> 01:14:01.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the government began to invest in the economy

asr-000767
01:14:01.080 --> 01:14:03.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while continuing to support economic recovery

asr-000768
01:14:03.080 --> 01:14:06.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and investing in the country's long-term growth.

asr-000769
01:14:06.080 --> 01:14:08.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As a response,

asr-000770
01:14:08.080 --> 01:14:15.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we crafted the country's medium-term fiscal framework in 2022.

asr-000771
01:14:15.080 --> 01:14:20.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The government's blueprint for gradually reducing our deficit and debt

asr-000772
01:14:20.080 --> 01:14:22.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while creating more jobs,

asr-000773
01:14:22.080 --> 01:14:24.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: increasing people's incomes,

asr-000774
01:14:24.080 --> 01:14:26.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and reducing poverty.

asr-000775
01:14:26.080 --> 01:14:31.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It set us on a path of gradual and sustained fiscal consolidation

asr-000776
01:14:31.080 --> 01:14:33.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to restore fiscal space

asr-000777
01:14:33.080 --> 01:14:36.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while continuing to invest in the foundations of growth.

asr-000778
01:14:36.080 --> 01:14:41.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But our recovery has not happened in an easy environment.

asr-000779
01:14:41.080 --> 01:14:42.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Over the years,

asr-000780
01:14:42.080 --> 01:14:44.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: external pressures and global uncertainties

asr-000781
01:14:44.080 --> 01:14:48.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: have disrupted supply chains and pushed inflation up,

asr-000782
01:14:48.080 --> 01:14:51.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: affecting the pace of growth.

asr-000783
01:14:51.080 --> 01:14:52.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In this context,

asr-000784
01:14:52.080 --> 01:14:55.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we had to recalibrate our growth and fiscal targets

asr-000785
01:14:55.080 --> 01:14:58.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to keep them realistic and responsive

asr-000786
01:14:58.080 --> 01:15:00.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to evolving economic conditions.

asr-000787
01:15:00.080 --> 01:15:03.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But the direction of our fiscal policy

asr-000788
01:15:03.080 --> 01:15:06.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: has remained consistent.

asr-000789
01:15:06.080 --> 01:15:09.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The administration has remained committed

asr-000790
01:15:09.080 --> 01:15:11.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to the path of fiscal consolidation

asr-000791
01:15:11.080 --> 01:15:13.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: with the goal of bringing down

asr-000792
01:15:13.080 --> 01:15:16.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the deficit to GDP ratio

asr-000793
01:15:16.080 --> 01:15:19.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from 5.4% this year

asr-000794
01:15:19.080 --> 01:15:22.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to just 3.5% by 2030

asr-000795
01:15:22.080 --> 01:15:24.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while supporting growth.

asr-000796
01:15:25.080 --> 01:15:28.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: To stay the course amid growing political tensions

asr-000797
01:15:28.080 --> 01:15:31.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and the need to fund the government's priority programs

asr-000798
01:15:31.080 --> 01:15:33.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: without relying on new taxes,

asr-000799
01:15:33.080 --> 01:15:36.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we strengthened revenues.

asr-000800
01:15:36.080 --> 01:15:39.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Total revenues grew double digits

asr-000801
01:15:39.080 --> 01:15:42.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: at an annual average of 10.5%

asr-000802
01:15:42.080 --> 01:15:45.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: over the last four years.

asr-000803
01:15:45.080 --> 01:15:48.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As tax revenues likewise increased

asr-000804
01:15:48.080 --> 01:15:51.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: by an average of 10.47%

asr-000805
01:15:51.080 --> 01:15:53.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: over the same period.

asr-000806
01:15:53.080 --> 01:15:54.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And finally,

asr-000807
01:15:54.080 --> 01:15:57.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: for the first time in history,

asr-000808
01:15:57.080 --> 01:15:59.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in 2025,

asr-000809
01:15:59.080 --> 01:16:02.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the BIR surpassed 3 trillion pesos

asr-000810
01:16:02.080 --> 01:16:05.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in tax collections.

asr-000811
01:16:05.080 --> 01:16:08.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And we continue to stay the course

asr-000812
01:16:08.080 --> 01:16:11.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to meet our fiscal program for the year.

asr-000813
01:16:11.080 --> 01:16:13.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As of June 2026,

asr-000814
01:16:13.080 --> 01:16:16.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we have reached 49.7%

asr-000815
01:16:16.080 --> 01:16:19.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of our full-year target.

asr-000816
01:16:19.080 --> 01:16:22.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Despite global shocks and external pressures,

asr-000817
01:16:22.080 --> 01:16:26.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: tax collections reached 2.14 trillion pesos

asr-000818
01:16:26.080 --> 01:16:28.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the first half of the year,

asr-000819
01:16:28.080 --> 01:16:33.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 5.4% higher than the same period last year.

asr-000820
01:16:33.080 --> 01:16:37.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The robust revenue performance

asr-000821
01:16:37.080 --> 01:16:40.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: at 16.6% of GDP

asr-000822
01:16:40.080 --> 01:16:44.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is among the highest in Southeast Asia.

asr-000823
01:16:44.080 --> 01:16:48.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This reflects the continued efforts

asr-000824
01:16:48.080 --> 01:16:50.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of the BIR and BOC

asr-000825
01:16:50.080 --> 01:16:52.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to strengthen collection,

asr-000826
01:16:52.080 --> 01:16:54.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: improve compliance,

asr-000827
01:16:54.080 --> 01:16:56.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and plug leakages.

asr-000828
01:16:56.080 --> 01:16:58.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As you can see from the slide,

asr-000829
01:16:58.080 --> 01:17:01.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the Philippines at 16.6%

asr-000830
01:17:01.080 --> 01:17:04.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: revenue effort is better than Malaysia,

asr-000831
01:17:04.080 --> 01:17:07.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Singapore, Thailand, and Indonesia.

asr-000832
01:17:07.080 --> 01:17:10.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The Bureau of Customs,

asr-000833
01:17:10.080 --> 01:17:12.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in particular this year,

asr-000834
01:17:12.080 --> 01:17:15.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is on track to reach the 1 trillion peso mark

asr-000835
01:17:15.080 --> 01:17:17.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in collections.

asr-000836
01:17:17.080 --> 01:17:20.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: With the BIR and BOC's

asr-000837
01:17:20.080 --> 01:17:22.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: continued strong performance,

asr-000838
01:17:22.080 --> 01:17:25.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we expect total national government tax revenues

asr-000839
01:17:25.080 --> 01:17:28.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to reach 4.4 trillion pesos

asr-000840
01:17:28.080 --> 01:17:31.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: by the end of 2026.

asr-000841
01:17:31.080 --> 01:17:36.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As the country's needs continue to grow,

asr-000842
01:17:36.080 --> 01:17:39.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we are also mobilizing additional sources of revenues

asr-000843
01:17:39.080 --> 01:17:42.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to help fund government priorities.

asr-000844
01:17:42.080 --> 01:17:45.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: One important source is the privatization

asr-000845
01:17:45.080 --> 01:17:48.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of idle or non-core government assets.

asr-000846
01:17:48.080 --> 01:17:49.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We privatized

asr-000847
01:17:49.080 --> 01:17:54.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the 797-megawatt Kaliraya-Botocan-Kalayaan

asr-000848
01:17:54.080 --> 01:17:57.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: hydroelectric power plant in 2025

asr-000849
01:17:57.080 --> 01:18:00.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: with 36.27 billion pesos

asr-000850
01:18:00.080 --> 01:18:05.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in sale proceeds accruing in 2026.

asr-000851
01:18:05.080 --> 01:18:07.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: These proceeds will be included

asr-000852
01:18:07.080 --> 01:18:09.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the calculation of PESOM's

asr-000853
01:18:09.080 --> 01:18:10.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: dividend remittance

asr-000854
01:18:10.080 --> 01:18:14.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to the national government in 2027.

asr-000855
01:18:14.080 --> 01:18:16.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In July 2026,

asr-000856
01:18:16.080 --> 01:18:17.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the DOF,

asr-000857
01:18:17.080 --> 01:18:18.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: through the Privatization

asr-000858
01:18:18.080 --> 01:18:20.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and Management Office,

asr-000859
01:18:20.080 --> 01:18:21.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: also successfully completed

asr-000860
01:18:21.080 --> 01:18:23.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the 1 billion peso sale

asr-000861
01:18:23.080 --> 01:18:25.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of government-owned properties

asr-000862
01:18:25.080 --> 01:18:27.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: at the atrium of Makati,

asr-000863
01:18:27.080 --> 01:18:31.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: covering 24 condominium units.

asr-000864
01:18:31.080 --> 01:18:33.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: These transactions demonstrate

asr-000865
01:18:33.080 --> 01:18:35.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: how we are unlocking value

asr-000866
01:18:35.080 --> 01:18:36.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from government assets

asr-000867
01:18:36.080 --> 01:18:38.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and ensuring that they support

asr-000868
01:18:38.080 --> 01:18:41.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the government's fiscal requirements.

asr-000869
01:18:41.080 --> 01:18:43.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In addition to privatization,

asr-000870
01:18:43.080 --> 01:18:45.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we are also maximizing returns

asr-000871
01:18:45.080 --> 01:18:46.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from government-owned

asr-000872
01:18:46.080 --> 01:18:48.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: or controlled corporations.

asr-000873
01:18:48.080 --> 01:18:49.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This year,

asr-000874
01:18:49.080 --> 01:18:51.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: as we have last year,

asr-000875
01:18:51.080 --> 01:18:53.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we have called on GOCCs

asr-000876
01:18:53.080 --> 01:18:55.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to continue remitting dividends

asr-000877
01:18:55.080 --> 01:18:58.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: at 75% of their annual net earnings

asr-000878
01:18:58.080 --> 01:19:02.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to the national government.

asr-000879
01:19:02.080 --> 01:19:05.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Disbursements for the first half of 2026

asr-000880
01:19:05.080 --> 01:19:08.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: amounted to 3.175 trillion

asr-000881
01:19:08.080 --> 01:19:11.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: or 49% of the full program.

asr-000882
01:19:11.080 --> 01:19:13.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As resources are limited

asr-000883
01:19:13.080 --> 01:19:16.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and the country's needs continue to grow,

asr-000884
01:19:16.080 --> 01:19:17.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we must be more deliberate

asr-000885
01:19:17.080 --> 01:19:19.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in directing public funds

asr-000886
01:19:19.080 --> 01:19:22.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: towards higher quality expenditures

asr-000887
01:19:22.080 --> 01:19:25.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: with greater multiplier effects.

asr-000888
01:19:25.080 --> 01:19:28.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Those that strengthen productive capacity,

asr-000889
01:19:28.080 --> 01:19:31.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: stimulate economic activity,

asr-000890
01:19:31.080 --> 01:19:33.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and deliver long-term benefits

asr-000891
01:19:33.080 --> 01:19:35.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to the people.

asr-000892
01:19:35.080 --> 01:19:37.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The objective is not to spend less,

asr-000893
01:19:37.080 --> 01:19:40.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: it is to spend better.

asr-000894
01:19:40.080 --> 01:19:42.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Because of these efforts,

asr-000895
01:19:42.080 --> 01:19:44.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: our fiscal deficit

asr-000896
01:19:44.080 --> 01:19:46.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: has continued to narrow.

asr-000897
01:19:46.080 --> 01:19:50.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: From 8.6% in 2021

asr-000898
01:19:50.080 --> 01:19:54.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and 7.3% in 2022,

asr-000899
01:19:54.080 --> 01:19:56.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we have consistently brought down

asr-000900
01:19:56.080 --> 01:19:58.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the fiscal deficit

asr-000901
01:19:58.080 --> 01:20:00.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to 5.6%

asr-000902
01:20:00.080 --> 01:20:03.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: over the last four years.

asr-000903
01:20:06.080 --> 01:20:08.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And we continue to make progress

asr-000904
01:20:08.080 --> 01:20:09.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: this 2026

asr-000905
01:20:09.080 --> 01:20:10.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: despite the economic shocks

asr-000906
01:20:10.080 --> 01:20:11.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: that we have faced,

asr-000907
01:20:11.080 --> 01:20:13.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: including those arising

asr-000908
01:20:13.080 --> 01:20:15.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from the conflict in the Middle East.

asr-000909
01:20:15.080 --> 01:20:17.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In the first half,

asr-000910
01:20:17.080 --> 01:20:19.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: our deficit-to-GDP ratio

asr-000911
01:20:19.080 --> 01:20:22.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: improved to 5.46%

asr-000912
01:20:22.080 --> 01:20:25.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: compared with 5.65%

asr-000913
01:20:25.080 --> 01:20:28.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the same period last year.

asr-000914
01:20:28.080 --> 01:20:29.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And we remain on track

asr-000915
01:20:29.080 --> 01:20:31.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to meet our fiscal deficit target

asr-000916
01:20:31.080 --> 01:20:34.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: for 2026.

asr-000917
01:20:34.080 --> 01:20:37.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We project a deficit-to-GDP ratio

asr-000918
01:20:37.080 --> 01:20:38.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of 5.44%

asr-000919
01:20:38.080 --> 01:20:41.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the second half of 2026,

asr-000920
01:20:41.080 --> 01:20:43.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: bringing the full year

asr-000921
01:20:43.080 --> 01:20:45.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to 5.45%

asr-000922
01:20:45.080 --> 01:20:48.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: our lowest deficit-to-GDP ratio

asr-000923
01:20:48.080 --> 01:20:50.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: since the start of the administration.

asr-000924
01:20:50.080 --> 01:20:52.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This continued reduction

asr-000925
01:20:52.080 --> 01:20:53.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the deficit

asr-000926
01:20:53.080 --> 01:20:55.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is an important indicator

asr-000927
01:20:55.080 --> 01:20:57.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: that the fiscal discipline

asr-000928
01:20:57.080 --> 01:20:58.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we are pursuing

asr-000929
01:20:58.080 --> 01:21:00.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is translating into concrete results.

asr-000930
01:21:00.080 --> 01:21:03.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And because we continue to manage

asr-000931
01:21:03.080 --> 01:21:05.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: our fiscal deficit responsibly,

asr-000932
01:21:05.080 --> 01:21:08.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: our debt levels remain sustainable.

asr-000933
01:21:08.080 --> 01:21:11.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In 2025,

asr-000934
01:21:11.080 --> 01:21:13.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the national government debt

asr-000935
01:21:13.080 --> 01:21:17.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: stood at 63.2% of GDP,

asr-000936
01:21:17.080 --> 01:21:20.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while the general government debt

asr-000937
01:21:20.080 --> 01:21:25.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: finished at 56.8% of GDP,

asr-000938
01:21:25.080 --> 01:21:29.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: well below the 70% international benchmark

asr-000939
01:21:29.080 --> 01:21:31.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: by the World Bank

asr-000940
01:21:31.080 --> 01:21:33.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: for debt sustainability

asr-000941
01:21:33.080 --> 01:21:35.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and within a manageable range

asr-000942
01:21:35.080 --> 01:21:39.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: compared to other emerging economies.

asr-000943
01:21:39.080 --> 01:21:42.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Just a point I'd like to raise

asr-000944
01:21:42.080 --> 01:21:45.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: or stress is that

asr-000945
01:21:45.080 --> 01:21:48.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the definition of the 70% threshold

asr-000946
01:21:48.080 --> 01:21:51.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is based on general government debt

asr-000947
01:21:51.080 --> 01:21:52.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to GDP,

asr-000948
01:21:52.080 --> 01:21:57.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: which we are at 56.8%.

asr-000949
01:21:57.080 --> 01:21:58.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: More importantly,

asr-000950
01:21:58.080 --> 01:21:59.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: on our debt,

asr-000951
01:21:59.080 --> 01:22:00.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we have maintained

asr-000952
01:22:00.080 --> 01:22:03.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: a prudent debt mix,

asr-000953
01:22:03.080 --> 01:22:06.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: predominantly domestic debt,

asr-000954
01:22:06.080 --> 01:22:08.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: predominantly carrying

asr-000955
01:22:08.080 --> 01:22:11.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: fixed interest rates,

asr-000956
01:22:11.080 --> 01:22:13.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and predominantly structured

asr-000957
01:22:13.080 --> 01:22:16.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: with long repayment terms.

asr-000958
01:22:16.080 --> 01:22:17.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: First,

asr-000959
01:22:17.080 --> 01:22:20.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 67% of our outstanding debt

asr-000960
01:22:20.080 --> 01:22:21.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is domestic.

asr-000961
01:22:21.080 --> 01:22:23.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This reduces our exposure

asr-000962
01:22:23.080 --> 01:22:25.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to foreign exchange risks,

asr-000963
01:22:25.080 --> 01:22:26.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while also supporting

asr-000964
01:22:26.080 --> 01:22:27.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the continued development

asr-000965
01:22:27.080 --> 01:22:30.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of our local capital market.

asr-000966
01:22:30.080 --> 01:22:32.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Second,

asr-000967
01:22:32.080 --> 01:22:33.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 90% of our debt

asr-000968
01:22:33.080 --> 01:22:36.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: carries fixed interest rates.

asr-000969
01:22:36.080 --> 01:22:38.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This provides greater certainty

asr-000970
01:22:38.080 --> 01:22:40.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in our debt servicing costs

asr-000971
01:22:40.080 --> 01:22:43.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and shields us from sudden increases

asr-000972
01:22:43.080 --> 01:22:48.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: or fluctuations in global interest rates.

asr-000973
01:22:48.080 --> 01:22:49.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And third,

asr-000974
01:22:49.080 --> 01:22:52.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 84.1% of our debt

asr-000975
01:22:52.080 --> 01:22:55.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: has long-term repayment periods,

asr-000976
01:22:55.080 --> 01:22:57.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: meaning we have several years

asr-000977
01:22:57.080 --> 01:23:00.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: before these obligations fall due.

asr-000978
01:23:00.080 --> 01:23:02.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This longer maturity profile

asr-000979
01:23:02.080 --> 01:23:04.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: reduces our refinancing risks

asr-000980
01:23:04.080 --> 01:23:06.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and gives us greater predictability

asr-000981
01:23:06.080 --> 01:23:09.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in managing our debt obligations.

asr-000982
01:23:10.080 --> 01:23:13.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This strategic borrowing mix

asr-000983
01:23:13.080 --> 01:23:15.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: by our Bureau of Treasury

asr-000984
01:23:15.080 --> 01:23:17.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: strengthens our resilience

asr-000985
01:23:17.080 --> 01:23:18.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to external shocks

asr-000986
01:23:18.080 --> 01:23:20.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and makes our debt obligations

asr-000987
01:23:20.080 --> 01:23:22.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: more predictable and manageable

asr-000988
01:23:22.080 --> 01:23:24.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: over the long term.

asr-000989
01:23:24.080 --> 01:23:28.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And the market,

asr-000990
01:23:28.080 --> 01:23:30.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the global markets assessment

asr-000991
01:23:30.080 --> 01:23:31.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of our fiscal fundamentals

asr-000992
01:23:31.080 --> 01:23:33.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is also reflected

asr-000993
01:23:33.080 --> 01:23:34.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the confidence

asr-000994
01:23:34.080 --> 01:23:38.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of international investors.

asr-000995
01:23:38.080 --> 01:23:40.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Our sovereign credit

asr-000996
01:23:40.080 --> 01:23:41.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: ratings remain

asr-000997
01:23:41.080 --> 01:23:43.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: at investment-grade levels.

asr-000998
01:23:43.080 --> 01:23:45.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We have two A-minus ratings

asr-000999
01:23:45.080 --> 01:23:48.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from Japanese credit rating agencies

asr-001000
01:23:48.080 --> 01:23:51.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and the equivalent of BBB

asr-001001
01:23:51.080 --> 01:23:53.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: or BBB Plus

asr-001002
01:23:53.080 --> 01:23:56.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from the global rating agencies.

asr-001003
01:23:56.080 --> 01:23:59.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This reflects continued confidence

asr-001004
01:23:59.080 --> 01:24:01.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the country's economic fundamentals

asr-001005
01:24:01.080 --> 01:24:03.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and our capacity

asr-001006
01:24:03.080 --> 01:24:06.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to manage our public's finances.

asr-001007
01:24:06.080 --> 01:24:08.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Higher credit ratings reflect

asr-001008
01:24:08.080 --> 01:24:10.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: minimal default risk

asr-001009
01:24:10.080 --> 01:24:12.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: signaling lenders to offer

asr-001010
01:24:12.080 --> 01:24:14.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: lower interest rates.

asr-001011
01:24:14.080 --> 01:24:15.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: When the country can borrow

asr-001012
01:24:15.080 --> 01:24:17.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: at lower interest rates,

asr-001013
01:24:17.080 --> 01:24:20.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: private businesses and consumers

asr-001014
01:24:20.080 --> 01:24:21.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: can also borrow

asr-001015
01:24:21.080 --> 01:24:23.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: at lower interest rates.

asr-001016
01:24:26.080 --> 01:24:28.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We have also seen progress

asr-001017
01:24:28.080 --> 01:24:29.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in our integration

asr-001018
01:24:29.080 --> 01:24:31.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: into global capital markets.

asr-001019
01:24:31.080 --> 01:24:33.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: With the upcoming historic debut

asr-001020
01:24:33.080 --> 01:24:35.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of our peso-denominated

asr-001021
01:24:35.080 --> 01:24:36.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: government bonds

asr-001022
01:24:36.080 --> 01:24:38.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the J.P. Morgan's

asr-001023
01:24:38.080 --> 01:24:39.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Government Bond Index,

asr-001024
01:24:39.080 --> 01:24:41.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we will be the first

asr-001025
01:24:41.080 --> 01:24:42.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: government bond index

asr-001026
01:24:42.080 --> 01:24:43.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: emerging markets

asr-001027
01:24:43.080 --> 01:24:45.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in January 2027.

asr-001028
01:24:45.080 --> 01:24:46.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This is significant

asr-001029
01:24:46.080 --> 01:24:49.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: because this is our first-ever inclusion

asr-001030
01:24:49.080 --> 01:24:52.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in a major global bond index.

asr-001031
01:24:52.080 --> 01:24:53.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And again,

asr-001032
01:24:53.080 --> 01:24:54.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: this reflects a strong

asr-001033
01:24:54.080 --> 01:24:55.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: vote of confidence

asr-001034
01:24:55.080 --> 01:24:57.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in our solid fundamentals

asr-001035
01:24:57.080 --> 01:25:00.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and fiscal discipline.

asr-001036
01:25:00.080 --> 01:25:02.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As we widen our investor base,

asr-001037
01:25:02.080 --> 01:25:03.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: this will strengthen demand

asr-001038
01:25:03.080 --> 01:25:06.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: for Philippine government securities,

asr-001039
01:25:06.080 --> 01:25:08.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: improve market liquidity,

asr-001040
01:25:08.080 --> 01:25:10.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: support the development

asr-001041
01:25:10.080 --> 01:25:11.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of our capital market,

asr-001042
01:25:11.080 --> 01:25:13.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and help lower borrowing costs

asr-001043
01:25:13.080 --> 01:25:18.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: for the government over time.

asr-001044
01:25:18.080 --> 01:25:21.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In 2027,

asr-001045
01:25:21.080 --> 01:25:23.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: when we project borrowing requirements

asr-001046
01:25:23.080 --> 01:25:26.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to reach 3.3 trillion pesos,

asr-001047
01:25:26.080 --> 01:25:28.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we will carry the same principles

asr-001048
01:25:28.080 --> 01:25:30.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of our debt strategy

asr-001049
01:25:30.080 --> 01:25:32.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: into our borrowing program

asr-001050
01:25:32.080 --> 01:25:35.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and make it even more sustainable.

asr-001051
01:25:35.080 --> 01:25:37.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We are increasing the share

asr-001052
01:25:37.080 --> 01:25:39.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of domestic borrowing

asr-001053
01:25:39.080 --> 01:25:43.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to 72%,

asr-001054
01:25:43.080 --> 01:25:45.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: which means around 2.4 trillion pesos

asr-001055
01:25:45.080 --> 01:25:46.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: will be sourced

asr-001056
01:25:46.080 --> 01:25:48.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from the domestic market,

asr-001057
01:25:48.080 --> 01:25:50.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while the remaining 28%,

asr-001058
01:25:50.080 --> 01:25:52.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: or around 915 billion,

asr-001059
01:25:52.080 --> 01:25:55.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: will come from external sources,

asr-001060
01:25:55.080 --> 01:25:59.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: such as loans and global bonds.

asr-001061
01:25:59.080 --> 01:26:00.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This borrowing strategy

asr-001062
01:26:00.080 --> 01:26:01.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: allows us to keep

asr-001063
01:26:01.080 --> 01:26:03.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the cost of borrowing low

asr-001064
01:26:03.080 --> 01:26:05.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while helping broaden

asr-001065
01:26:05.080 --> 01:26:06.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: our investor base,

asr-001066
01:26:06.080 --> 01:26:07.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: maintain access

asr-001067
01:26:07.080 --> 01:26:09.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to key international markets,

asr-001068
01:26:09.080 --> 01:26:11.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and support the continued development

asr-001069
01:26:11.080 --> 01:26:13.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of our local bond market.

asr-001070
01:26:16.080 --> 01:26:19.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: With tax collections projected to grow

asr-001071
01:26:19.080 --> 01:26:21.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: by an average of 9% annually

asr-001072
01:26:21.080 --> 01:26:24.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from 2026 to 2028,

asr-001073
01:26:24.080 --> 01:26:25.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: total revenues is targeted

asr-001074
01:26:25.080 --> 01:26:28.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to reach 5.5 trillion pesos

asr-001075
01:26:28.080 --> 01:26:31.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: by the end of the President's term.

asr-001076
01:26:31.080 --> 01:26:32.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: By 2030,

asr-001077
01:26:32.080 --> 01:26:34.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we expect total revenues

asr-001078
01:26:34.080 --> 01:26:36.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to exceed 6 trillion.

asr-001079
01:26:36.080 --> 01:26:39.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This means our revenue agencies

asr-001080
01:26:39.080 --> 01:26:40.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: will have to raise the bar

asr-001081
01:26:40.080 --> 01:26:41.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: even further.

asr-001082
01:26:41.080 --> 01:26:43.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The BIR and BOC

asr-001083
01:26:43.080 --> 01:26:44.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: will need to continue

asr-001084
01:26:44.080 --> 01:26:46.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: improving efficiency,

asr-001085
01:26:46.080 --> 01:26:48.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: strengthening compliance,

asr-001086
01:26:48.080 --> 01:26:49.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and leveraging technology

asr-001087
01:26:49.080 --> 01:26:51.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to sustain faster growth

asr-001088
01:26:51.080 --> 01:26:52.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in collections.

asr-001089
01:26:52.080 --> 01:26:54.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Coupled with stronger

asr-001090
01:26:54.080 --> 01:26:55.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: collection efforts,

asr-001091
01:26:55.080 --> 01:26:57.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we are looking to pursue reforms

asr-001092
01:26:57.080 --> 01:26:59.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: that will make our revenue system

asr-001093
01:26:59.080 --> 01:27:00.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: more efficient,

asr-001094
01:27:00.080 --> 01:27:01.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: equitable,

asr-001095
01:27:01.080 --> 01:27:03.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and sustainable.

asr-001096
01:27:03.080 --> 01:27:05.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We are promoting growth

asr-001097
01:27:05.080 --> 01:27:07.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: revenue and equity

asr-001098
01:27:07.080 --> 01:27:10.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: towards socio-economic stability,

asr-001099
01:27:10.080 --> 01:27:11.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: sustainability,

asr-001100
01:27:11.080 --> 01:27:13.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: or progress

asr-001101
01:27:13.080 --> 01:27:15.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: through a comprehensive reform package

asr-001102
01:27:15.080 --> 01:27:18.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: that provides targeted tax relief

asr-001103
01:27:18.080 --> 01:27:20.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while strengthening revenues

asr-001104
01:27:20.080 --> 01:27:22.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from products with social,

asr-001105
01:27:22.080 --> 01:27:23.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: environmental,

asr-001106
01:27:23.080 --> 01:27:25.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and health costs.

asr-001107
01:27:26.080 --> 01:27:28.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We likewise expect more revenues

asr-001108
01:27:28.080 --> 01:27:29.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from the proposed

asr-001109
01:27:29.080 --> 01:27:31.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: multinational minimum tax bill,

asr-001110
01:27:31.080 --> 01:27:34.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: which will preserve our taxing rights

asr-001111
01:27:34.080 --> 01:27:36.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and ensure that taxes arising

asr-001112
01:27:36.080 --> 01:27:37.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from economic activity

asr-001113
01:27:37.080 --> 01:27:38.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the Philippines

asr-001114
01:27:38.080 --> 01:27:40.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: are collected here.

asr-001115
01:27:40.080 --> 01:27:44.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And the General Tax Amnesty Bill

asr-001116
01:27:44.080 --> 01:27:47.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: mentioned by the President in his SONA

asr-001117
01:27:47.080 --> 01:27:48.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to encourage the settlement

asr-001118
01:27:48.080 --> 01:27:50.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of outstanding tax obligations,

asr-001119
01:27:50.080 --> 01:27:52.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: improve compliance,

asr-001120
01:27:52.080 --> 01:27:53.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and bring more taxpayers

asr-001121
01:27:53.080 --> 01:27:56.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: into the formal tax system.

asr-001122
01:27:56.080 --> 01:28:00.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Disbursements will grow moderately

asr-001123
01:28:00.080 --> 01:28:02.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from 2026 to 2028.

asr-001124
01:28:02.080 --> 01:28:04.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We must be more deliberate

asr-001125
01:28:04.080 --> 01:28:06.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: about where we put our resources,

asr-001126
01:28:06.080 --> 01:28:08.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: prioritizing investments

asr-001127
01:28:08.080 --> 01:28:10.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: that strengthen productive capacity,

asr-001128
01:28:10.080 --> 01:28:12.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: support long-term growth,

asr-001129
01:28:12.080 --> 01:28:14.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and deliver tangible benefits

asr-001130
01:28:14.080 --> 01:28:16.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to our people.

asr-001131
01:28:16.080 --> 01:28:18.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We must focus on programs

asr-001132
01:28:18.080 --> 01:28:19.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and investments that generate

asr-001133
01:28:19.080 --> 01:28:20.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the greatest economic

asr-001134
01:28:20.080 --> 01:28:22.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and social returns,

asr-001135
01:28:22.080 --> 01:28:25.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: particularly in critical infrastructure,

asr-001136
01:28:25.080 --> 01:28:26.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: health,

asr-001137
01:28:26.080 --> 01:28:27.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: education,

asr-001138
01:28:27.080 --> 01:28:28.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and other areas

asr-001139
01:28:28.080 --> 01:28:31.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: that support long-term growth.

asr-001140
01:28:31.080 --> 01:28:33.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As revenues grow faster

asr-001141
01:28:33.080 --> 01:28:35.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: than disbursements,

asr-001142
01:28:35.080 --> 01:28:37.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we see a clear and sustained path

asr-001143
01:28:37.080 --> 01:28:40.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: towards fiscal consolidation.

asr-001144
01:28:40.080 --> 01:28:42.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The deficit-to-GDP ratio

asr-001145
01:28:42.080 --> 01:28:44.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is projected to steadily decline

asr-001146
01:28:44.080 --> 01:28:47.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from 5.4% in 2026

asr-001147
01:28:47.080 --> 01:28:51.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to 3.5% by 2030,

asr-001148
01:28:51.080 --> 01:28:53.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: putting us on a progressively stronger

asr-001149
01:28:53.080 --> 01:28:57.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: fiscal footing through 2030.

asr-001150
01:28:57.080 --> 01:28:59.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This improving fiscal trajectory

asr-001151
01:28:59.080 --> 01:29:02.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is also reflected in our debt outlook.

asr-001152
01:29:02.080 --> 01:29:04.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: From 2026 to 2030,

asr-001153
01:29:04.080 --> 01:29:05.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: both national government

asr-001154
01:29:05.080 --> 01:29:07.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and general government debt ratios

asr-001155
01:29:07.080 --> 01:29:11.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: are projected to decrease gradually.

asr-001156
01:29:11.080 --> 01:29:13.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: National government debt

asr-001157
01:29:13.080 --> 01:29:14.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is projected to ease

asr-001158
01:29:14.080 --> 01:29:19.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from 65% to 63% in 2030,

asr-001159
01:29:19.080 --> 01:29:21.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while general government debt

asr-001160
01:29:21.080 --> 01:29:22.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is expected to decline

asr-001161
01:29:22.080 --> 01:29:25.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from 59% to 56%

asr-001162
01:29:25.080 --> 01:29:28.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: over the same period.

asr-001163
01:29:28.080 --> 01:29:30.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As we look ahead,

asr-001164
01:29:30.080 --> 01:29:31.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the path we had laid out

asr-001165
01:29:31.080 --> 01:29:33.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is clear.

asr-001166
01:29:33.080 --> 01:29:34.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We assure the honorable members

asr-001167
01:29:34.080 --> 01:29:35.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of this Chamber

asr-001168
01:29:35.080 --> 01:29:36.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: that the economic team

asr-001169
01:29:36.080 --> 01:29:38.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: will continue to strengthen revenues,

asr-001170
01:29:38.080 --> 01:29:41.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: manage expenditures responsibly,

asr-001171
01:29:41.080 --> 01:29:43.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: reduce the deficit,

asr-001172
01:29:43.080 --> 01:29:44.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and keep our debt

asr-001173
01:29:44.080 --> 01:29:46.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: on a sustainable path.

asr-001174
01:29:46.080 --> 01:29:47.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: At the same time,

asr-001175
01:29:47.080 --> 01:29:48.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we are building fiscal buffers

asr-001176
01:29:48.080 --> 01:29:50.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: that will give us room

asr-001177
01:29:50.080 --> 01:29:52.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to respond to future shocks

asr-001178
01:29:52.080 --> 01:29:53.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: without compromising

asr-001179
01:29:53.080 --> 01:29:56.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: our long-term fiscal sustainability.

asr-001180
01:29:56.080 --> 01:29:57.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We look forward

asr-001181
01:29:57.080 --> 01:29:59.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to working closely with Congress

asr-001182
01:29:59.080 --> 01:30:00.000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to ensure that

asr-001183
01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:04.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: ensure that the government lives within its means.

asr-001184
01:30:04.460 --> 01:30:10.380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This means making difficult choices, prioritizing programs and investments with the greatest

asr-001185
01:30:10.380 --> 01:30:19.420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: impact, and ensuring that new spending commitments are matched by sustainable sources of funding.

asr-001186
01:30:19.420 --> 01:30:25.280
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Most importantly, let us continue to ensure that every peso of public fund works for the

asr-001187
01:30:25.280 --> 01:30:27.900
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Filipino people.

asr-001188
01:30:27.900 --> 01:30:32.660
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And our national budget can work harder when we invest in programs and projects that can

asr-001189
01:30:32.660 --> 01:30:36.020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: help shape our future.

asr-001190
01:30:36.020 --> 01:30:40.020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The government must continue to address the immediate needs of our people, but we must

asr-001191
01:30:40.020 --> 01:30:47.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: look beyond the present and invest in higher, multiplier programs and projects that create

asr-001192
01:30:47.780 --> 01:30:54.480
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: lasting economic value, those that create jobs, raise incomes, and build a stronger

asr-001193
01:30:54.480 --> 01:30:57.220
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: economy tomorrow.

asr-001194
01:30:57.220 --> 01:30:57.880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Well-chosen

asr-001195
01:30:57.880 --> 01:31:03.160
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: infrastructure, for example, does more than address today's needs.

asr-001196
01:31:03.160 --> 01:31:09.220
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It can generate economic activity, connect communities, attract private investment, and

asr-001197
01:31:09.220 --> 01:31:13.340
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: deliver benefits for many years to come.

asr-001198
01:31:13.340 --> 01:31:19.180
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Let us work together to make the 2027 National Budget count and ensure that its benefits

asr-001199
01:31:19.180 --> 01:31:22.280
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: ripple through generations.

asr-001200
01:31:22.280 --> 01:31:26.000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This is the fiscal discipline we owe to the Filipino people.

asr-001201
01:31:26.000 --> 01:31:27.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Maraming salamat po.

asr-001202
01:31:27.880 --> 01:31:33.160
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you very much, Secretary Frederick Go, for that presentation.

asr-001203
01:31:33.160 --> 01:31:37.380
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We will now move to the final presentation.

asr-001204
01:31:37.380 --> 01:31:41.700
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: From the Department of Budget and Management, may now recognize the Honorable Secretary Kim

asr-001205
01:31:41.700 --> 01:31:43.260
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Robert C. de Leon.

asr-001206
01:31:43.260 --> 01:31:52.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: To House Speaker Bodjie Dy III, the Majority Leader, the Minority Leader, House

asr-001207
01:31:52.420 --> 01:31:56.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Committee on Appropriations Chairperson Mikaela Angela Suansing, Vice Chairwoman Angela D.

asr-001208
01:31:56.160 --> 01:32:01.740
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Suansing, Vice Chairpersons of the Committee on Appropriations, Honorable Members of the

asr-001209
01:32:01.740 --> 01:32:11.500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 20th Congress, my fellow economic managers and colleagues in government, isang mapagpalang araw po sa ating lahat. As acting Secretary

asr-001210
01:32:11.500 --> 01:32:16.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of the Department of Budget and Management and Chair of the Development Budget Coordination

asr-001211
01:32:16.600 --> 01:32:23.200
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Committee, it is my honor to present the key dimensions and priorities of the Fiscal Year

asr-001212
01:32:23.200 --> 01:32:26.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 2027 National Expenditure Program.

asr-001213
01:32:26.000 --> 01:32:26.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Thank you.

asr-001214
01:32:26.040 --> 01:32:27.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Thank you, Secretary.

asr-001215
01:32:27.040 --> 01:32:28.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Thank you, Secretary.

asr-001216
01:32:28.040 --> 01:32:29.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Thank you, Secretary.

asr-001217
01:32:29.040 --> 01:32:30.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Thank you.

asr-001218
01:32:30.040 --> 01:32:31.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Thank you.

asr-001219
01:32:31.040 --> 01:32:32.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Let us now begin.

asr-001220
01:32:32.040 --> 01:32:33.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The National Expenditure Program.

asr-001221
01:32:33.040 --> 01:32:34.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Today, we are not simply presenting a 7.2 trillion peso spending plan.

asr-001222
01:32:34.040 --> 01:32:39.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are presenting the results of months of careful review, difficult choices and rigorous

asr-001223
01:32:39.160 --> 01:32:46.500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: prioritization, determining what government must fund, what the country urgently needs,

asr-001224
01:32:46.500 --> 01:32:52.840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: what agencies are ready to implement and what our fiscal space can responsibly support.

asr-001225
01:32:52.840 --> 01:32:55.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: With the theme of People-Centered Grants.

asr-001226
01:32:55.880 --> 01:33:02.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: growth for an inclusive and resilient future the proposed national budget reflects our vision of

asr-001227
01:33:02.360 --> 01:33:09.240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: economic growth that is measured not only by stronger macroeconomic indicators but ultimately

asr-001228
01:33:09.240 --> 01:33:16.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: by better lives for every filipino this budget is the product of the tireless work and dedication

asr-001229
01:33:16.360 --> 01:33:21.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of our fellow public servants at the dbm and across the departments and agencies of the

asr-001230
01:33:21.960 --> 01:33:29.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: executive branch and let me emphasize that arriving at this budget was not a simple exercise

asr-001231
01:33:29.960 --> 01:33:40.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of adding up agency requests for fiscal year 2027 we received more than 11 trillion pesos in budget

asr-001232
01:33:40.360 --> 01:33:48.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: proposals from different government agencies for possible inclusion in the nep but our total

asr-001233
01:33:48.440 --> 01:33:51.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: expenditure program is 7.2 trillion

asr-001234
01:33:51.960 --> 01:33:59.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: pesos clearly we could not accommodate every request we therefore had to carefully and

asr-001235
01:33:59.880 --> 01:34:06.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: thoroughly deliberate on these proposals looking at their alignment with the president's priorities

asr-001236
01:34:06.120 --> 01:34:13.640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: in the philippine development plan implementation readiness absorptive capacity and past performance

asr-001237
01:34:14.280 --> 01:34:20.280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: project maturity expected outcomes and overall value to the filipino people

asr-001238
01:34:21.080 --> 01:34:21.940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the nep is not the only project that has been implemented in the philippine development plan

asr-001239
01:34:21.940 --> 01:34:23.940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: implementation

asr-001240
01:34:23.940 --> 01:34:39.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the nep is not a compilation of everything government agencies asked for it is the result of choices and prioritization within the fiscal space available to government in simpler terms the nep is never a wish list it is a prioritized spending plan

asr-001241
01:34:40.260 --> 01:34:46.740
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: guided by the clear direction of our president every effort was made to ensure that this budget

asr-001242
01:34:46.740 --> 01:34:50.340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: delivers real and meaningful benefits to every filipino

asr-001243
01:34:50.900 --> 01:34:51.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: every region

asr-001244
01:34:51.940 --> 01:34:58.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and every community through to the spirit of our vision of bawat bayan maki kinabang

asr-001245
01:34:59.380 --> 01:35:07.540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the proposed 7.2 trillion peso national budget is equivalent to 21.7 percent of gdp

asr-001246
01:35:08.100 --> 01:35:17.300
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and is 407 billion peso or 6 higher than the fiscal year 2026 budget the bulk of the increase

asr-001247
01:35:17.300 --> 01:35:21.460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: comes from mandatory requirements and existing fiscal obligations

asr-001248
01:35:21.940 --> 01:35:26.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: including higher national tax allotment for our local government units,

asr-001249
01:35:26.380 --> 01:35:33.280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the fourth tranche of salary adjustment for civilian government employees under EO No. 64,

asr-001250
01:35:34.040 --> 01:35:38.260
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the corresponding salary adjustments for our military and uniformed personnel,

asr-001251
01:35:38.800 --> 01:35:42.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and our other fiscal obligations of the government.

asr-001252
01:35:42.740 --> 01:35:47.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: At the same time, we are making critical investments in people, infrastructure,

asr-001253
01:35:47.600 --> 01:35:52.340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: resilience, and public services to sustain economic growth.

asr-001254
01:35:53.100 --> 01:36:00.140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The 6% increase does not mean that every agency or every program received a corresponding increase.

asr-001255
01:36:00.820 --> 01:36:04.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Every peso still had to compete for limited fiscal space,

asr-001256
01:36:04.660 --> 01:36:08.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and every major expenditure had to be justified.

asr-001257
01:36:09.240 --> 01:36:13.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Fundamentally, this budget is people-centered, inclusive, and resilient.

asr-001258
01:36:13.580 --> 01:36:15.940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: It invests in every Filipino,

asr-001259
01:36:16.420 --> 01:36:17.460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: extends opportunities,

asr-001260
01:36:17.600 --> 01:36:19.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: contributes to every sector and every region,

asr-001261
01:36:19.600 --> 01:36:24.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and strengthens our nation's capacity to withstand future challenges

asr-001262
01:36:24.420 --> 01:36:28.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: so that progress is not only sustained but shared by all.

asr-001263
01:36:28.420 --> 01:36:30.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Guided by this vision,

asr-001264
01:36:30.420 --> 01:36:38.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: please allow me to present the dimensions and highlights of the Fiscal Year 2027 National Expenditure Program.

asr-001265
01:36:38.420 --> 01:36:40.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: First and foremost,

asr-001266
01:36:40.420 --> 01:36:46.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: this budget remains anchored in a disciplined, rules-based appropriations framework.

asr-001267
01:36:46.420 --> 01:36:47.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The proposed budget,

asr-001268
01:36:47.600 --> 01:36:49.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is composed of two main sources.

asr-001269
01:36:49.600 --> 01:36:54.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Programmed appropriations of 4.494 trillion pesos,

asr-001270
01:36:54.600 --> 01:37:00.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: which fund the priority programs, projects, and operations of government.

asr-001271
01:37:00.600 --> 01:37:06.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And automatic appropriations of 2.706 trillion pesos,

asr-001272
01:37:06.600 --> 01:37:11.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: which covers expenditures mandated under existing laws.

asr-001273
01:37:11.600 --> 01:37:15.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Among the major automatic appropriations are

asr-001274
01:37:15.600 --> 01:37:16.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 1.32 trillion pesos,

asr-001275
01:37:16.600 --> 01:37:17.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 1.32 trillion pesos,

asr-001276
01:37:17.600 --> 01:37:22.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for national tax allotment of local government units,

asr-001277
01:37:22.600 --> 01:37:25.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 1.114 trillion pesos,

asr-001278
01:37:25.600 --> 01:37:27.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for interest payments,

asr-001279
01:37:27.600 --> 01:37:30.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 104.2 billion pesos,

asr-001280
01:37:30.600 --> 01:37:36.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for the annual block grant of the Bangsamoro Autonomous Region in Musly, Mindanao,

asr-001281
01:37:36.600 --> 01:37:43.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and 89 billion for retirement and life insurance premiums of national government employees.

asr-001282
01:37:43.600 --> 01:37:46.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This demonstrates that a considerable portion

asr-001283
01:37:46.600 --> 01:37:52.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of the 7.2 trillion peso budget is already determined by laws,

asr-001284
01:37:52.600 --> 01:37:58.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: formula, and existing obligations before government even begins deciding

asr-001285
01:37:58.600 --> 01:38:01.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: which new or expanded programs to fund.

asr-001286
01:38:01.600 --> 01:38:03.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Meanwhile,

asr-001287
01:38:03.600 --> 01:38:09.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: unprogrammed appropriations have been significantly reduced to just 112 billion pesos,

asr-001288
01:38:09.600 --> 01:38:15.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the lowest NEP proposal nominally since 2019,

asr-001289
01:38:15.600 --> 01:38:21.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and at only 1.56% of the total expenditure program,

asr-001290
01:38:21.600 --> 01:38:29.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: likewise the lowest UA to total expenditure program ratio since 1991.

asr-001291
01:38:29.600 --> 01:38:33.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And for the benefit of our kababayans who are watching this briefing live,

asr-001292
01:38:33.600 --> 01:38:39.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: please allow me to note that the inclusion of unprogrammed appropriations in the budget

asr-001293
01:38:39.600 --> 01:38:43.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: does not mean that the amount is automatically available for release.

asr-001294
01:38:43.600 --> 01:38:48.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: It is a standby spending authority for specifically identified purposes

asr-001295
01:38:48.600 --> 01:38:54.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: that may be accessed only when the funding conditions prescribed by law are satisfied.

asr-001296
01:38:54.600 --> 01:38:57.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For fiscal year 2027,

asr-001297
01:38:57.600 --> 01:39:03.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the proposed UA has been deliberately narrowed primarily to finance,

asr-001298
01:39:03.600 --> 01:39:09.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: partially the restoration of the fund balance previously remitted by the Philippine Deposit Insurance Corporation,

asr-001299
01:39:09.600 --> 01:39:11.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: as well as to support foreign-assisted projects,

asr-001300
01:39:11.600 --> 01:39:19.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: which are still currently being assessed and evaluated by the Investment Coordination Committee

asr-001301
01:39:19.600 --> 01:39:23.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and eventually for approval by the ED Council.

asr-001302
01:39:23.600 --> 01:39:27.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This reflects the administration's conscious policy choice

asr-001303
01:39:27.600 --> 01:39:31.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to put more expenditures under programmed appropriations

asr-001304
01:39:31.600 --> 01:39:34.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: where funding is clearer and more predictable

asr-001305
01:39:34.600 --> 01:39:39.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: while keeping standby appropriations to the minimum necessary.

asr-001306
01:39:39.600 --> 01:39:41.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The proposed fiscal year 2027

asr-001307
01:39:41.600 --> 01:39:48.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: national budget was prepared on the basis of agencies' funding requirements

asr-001308
01:39:48.600 --> 01:39:54.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and with close consideration of their budget utilization and implementation capacity.

asr-001309
01:39:54.600 --> 01:39:58.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: As of June 30, 2026,

asr-001310
01:39:58.600 --> 01:40:04.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: total available appropriations had reached P7.54 trillion,

asr-001311
01:40:04.600 --> 01:40:10.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of which P6.63 trillion had already been released

asr-001312
01:40:10.600 --> 01:40:13.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: as allotments to various agencies,

asr-001313
01:40:13.600 --> 01:40:22.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: including P546.79 billion from continuing appropriations from fiscal year 2025.

asr-001314
01:40:22.600 --> 01:40:24.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Of these allotments,

asr-001315
01:40:24.600 --> 01:40:31.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: agencies had already obligated P3.29 trillion or 49.5%,

asr-001316
01:40:31.600 --> 01:40:38.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: comprising P3.13 trillion from fiscal year 2026 appropriations

asr-001317
01:40:38.600 --> 01:40:45.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and P158.58 billion from fiscal year 2025 continuing appropriations.

asr-001318
01:40:45.600 --> 01:40:48.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: In terms of disbursements,

asr-001319
01:40:48.600 --> 01:40:53.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 81.9% of the reported obligations have been paid.

asr-001320
01:40:53.600 --> 01:41:00.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Meanwhile, unreleased appropriations amounted to P820.21 billion

asr-001321
01:41:00.600 --> 01:41:05.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: as of June 30 from the fiscal year 2026 GAA

asr-001322
01:41:05.600 --> 01:41:07.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and P89.7 billion

asr-001323
01:41:07.600 --> 01:41:11.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: from fiscal year 2025 continuing appropriations.

asr-001324
01:41:11.600 --> 01:41:15.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: These data have guided our budget preparation process

asr-001325
01:41:15.600 --> 01:41:18.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and reinforced the need to align future allocations

asr-001326
01:41:18.600 --> 01:41:22.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: with agencies' implementation capacity.

asr-001327
01:41:22.600 --> 01:41:25.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This reflects our commitment to ensuring that budgets

asr-001328
01:41:25.600 --> 01:41:27.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: are not only approved and released,

asr-001329
01:41:27.600 --> 01:41:30.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: but effectively implemented,

asr-001330
01:41:30.600 --> 01:41:33.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: because every peso delivers its true value

asr-001331
01:41:33.600 --> 01:41:36.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: only when it is translated into timely,

asr-001332
01:41:36.600 --> 01:41:41.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: measurable, and meaningful outcomes for the Filipino people.

asr-001333
01:41:41.600 --> 01:41:43.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: By expense class,

asr-001334
01:41:43.600 --> 01:41:46.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the proposed fiscal year 2027 budget

asr-001335
01:41:46.600 --> 01:41:49.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: reflects a disciplined spending strategy

asr-001336
01:41:49.600 --> 01:41:52.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to sustain government operations,

asr-001337
01:41:52.600 --> 01:41:54.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: invest in long-term development,

asr-001338
01:41:54.600 --> 01:41:57.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and fulfill our fiscal obligations.

asr-001339
01:41:57.600 --> 01:42:02.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Maintenance and other operating expenses, or MOOE,

asr-001340
01:42:02.600 --> 01:42:05.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: will receive P2.944 trillion.

asr-001341
01:42:06.600 --> 01:42:07.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: In addition,

asr-001342
01:42:07.600 --> 01:42:09.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the proposed fiscal year 2027 budget

asr-001343
01:42:09.600 --> 01:42:13.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: reflects a 1.2% decrease from the fiscal year 2027 GAA

asr-001344
01:42:13.600 --> 01:42:17.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: despite the 6% overall increase in the national budget.

asr-001345
01:42:17.600 --> 01:42:19.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: In absolute terms,

asr-001346
01:42:19.600 --> 01:42:24.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: MOOE actually decreases by P36.2 billion.

asr-001347
01:42:24.600 --> 01:42:27.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This shows that growth of the budget is not driven

asr-001348
01:42:27.600 --> 01:42:32.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: by a broad expansion in operating expenditures.

asr-001349
01:42:32.600 --> 01:42:35.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We have allocated P1.982 trillion

asr-001350
01:42:35.600 --> 01:42:38.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for personnel services,

asr-001351
01:42:38.600 --> 01:42:41.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: an increase of P138.2 billion,

asr-001352
01:42:41.600 --> 01:42:43.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: or 7.5%,

asr-001353
01:42:43.600 --> 01:42:46.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to support the public servants who deliver education,

asr-001354
01:42:46.600 --> 01:42:49.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: health care, public safety, national defense,

asr-001355
01:42:49.600 --> 01:42:52.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and other essential services.

asr-001356
01:42:52.600 --> 01:42:55.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This also reflects salary adjustments

asr-001357
01:42:55.600 --> 01:42:57.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and other personnel requirements

asr-001358
01:42:57.600 --> 01:42:59.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: already committed by the government.

asr-001359
01:42:59.600 --> 01:43:04.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Notably, PS and MOOE remain fully covered

asr-001360
01:43:04.600 --> 01:43:07.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: by our projected revenues,

asr-001361
01:43:07.600 --> 01:43:11.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: reinforcing our commitment to fiscal discipline.

asr-001362
01:43:11.600 --> 01:43:17.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Meanwhile, capital outlays increased to P1.16 trillion,

asr-001363
01:43:17.600 --> 01:43:23.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: up by P140.8 billion, or 13.8%,

asr-001364
01:43:23.600 --> 01:43:27.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: allowing government to invest in infrastructure,

asr-001365
01:43:27.600 --> 01:43:30.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: equipment, facilities, and other assets

asr-001366
01:43:30.600 --> 01:43:33.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: with long-term economic and social value.

asr-001367
01:43:34.600 --> 01:43:38.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Financial expenses amount to P1.114 trillion,

asr-001368
01:43:38.600 --> 01:43:43.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: up by P164.3 billion, or 17.3%,

asr-001369
01:43:43.600 --> 01:43:47.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: primarily reflecting interest payments.

asr-001370
01:43:47.600 --> 01:43:49.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Allow me to briefly note the context

asr-001371
01:43:49.600 --> 01:43:51.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: behind the increase in interest payments.

asr-001372
01:43:51.600 --> 01:43:54.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: A higher interest bill does not by itself mean

asr-001373
01:43:54.600 --> 01:43:57.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: that our debt has become unmanageable.

asr-001374
01:43:57.600 --> 01:43:59.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Our debt remains manageable,

asr-001375
01:43:59.600 --> 01:44:02.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: as previously mentioned by the Secretary of Finance,

asr-001376
01:44:02.600 --> 01:44:06.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and debt servicing is explicitly provided for in the budget.

asr-001377
01:44:06.600 --> 01:44:10.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: At the same time, our medium-term fiscal program

asr-001378
01:44:10.600 --> 01:44:13.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is designed to gradually narrow the deficit

asr-001379
01:44:13.600 --> 01:44:15.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: while protecting growth-enhancing

asr-001380
01:44:15.600 --> 01:44:18.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and socially important expenditures.

asr-001381
01:44:18.600 --> 01:44:21.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Our approach is therefore not to sacrifice growth

asr-001382
01:44:21.600 --> 01:44:24.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: simply to reduce the deficit overnight.

asr-001383
01:44:24.600 --> 01:44:28.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are pursuing a strategic and gradual fiscal consolidation path

asr-001384
01:44:28.600 --> 01:44:31.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: that allows us to honor our obligations,

asr-001385
01:44:31.600 --> 01:44:33.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: maintain fiscal credibility,

asr-001386
01:44:33.600 --> 01:44:37.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and continue investing in our people and our economy.

asr-001387
01:44:37.600 --> 01:44:42.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The proposed national budget will be allocated across five sectors,

asr-001388
01:44:42.600 --> 01:44:46.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: with the largest share, P34.1%,

asr-001389
01:44:46.600 --> 01:44:51.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: or P2.456 trillion going to social services.

asr-001390
01:44:51.600 --> 01:44:55.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This finances investments that Filipinos encounter directly

asr-001391
01:44:55.600 --> 01:44:57.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: in their everyday lives.

asr-001392
01:44:57.600 --> 01:45:00.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Education, health, social protection,

asr-001393
01:45:00.600 --> 01:45:04.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: employment, housing, and other essential services.

asr-001394
01:45:04.600 --> 01:45:08.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Economic services will receive 25.5%,

asr-001395
01:45:08.600 --> 01:45:11.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: or P1.833 trillion,

asr-001396
01:45:11.600 --> 01:45:14.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: supporting infrastructure, agriculture,

asr-001397
01:45:14.600 --> 01:45:17.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: transportation, water resources,

asr-001398
01:45:17.600 --> 01:45:22.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: digital connectivity, and other productivity-enhancing investments.

asr-001399
01:45:22.600 --> 01:45:28.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: General public services will receive 18.3%,

asr-001400
01:45:28.600 --> 01:45:31.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: or P1.317 trillion,

asr-001401
01:45:31.600 --> 01:45:34.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: while defense will receive 6.3%,

asr-001402
01:45:34.600 --> 01:45:37.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: or P452.4 billion,

asr-001403
01:45:37.600 --> 01:45:41.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: as we strengthen our capacity to protect our territory,

asr-001404
01:45:41.600 --> 01:45:44.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: our communities, and our people.

asr-001405
01:45:44.600 --> 01:45:49.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Meanwhile, 15.9%, or P1.143 trillion,

asr-001406
01:45:49.600 --> 01:45:51.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is allocated for debt burden,

asr-001407
01:45:51.600 --> 01:45:54.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: covering interest payments and net lending

asr-001408
01:45:54.600 --> 01:45:56.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to government corporations.

asr-001409
01:45:56.600 --> 01:46:00.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Again, debt service should be viewed in its proper context.

asr-001410
01:46:00.600 --> 01:46:04.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Meeting our obligations protects the government's creditworthiness,

asr-001411
01:46:04.600 --> 01:46:06.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: preserves investor confidence,

asr-001412
01:46:06.600 --> 01:46:12.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and helps keep financing available for future public investments.

asr-001413
01:46:12.600 --> 01:46:14.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The important point is balance.

asr-001414
01:46:14.600 --> 01:46:17.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We honor what we owe while continuing to invest

asr-001415
01:46:17.600 --> 01:46:20.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: in what our people need.

asr-001416
01:46:20.600 --> 01:46:22.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: By recipient unit,

asr-001417
01:46:22.600 --> 01:46:25.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: national government agencies will receive the largest share

asr-001418
01:46:25.600 --> 01:46:28.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: at P4.332 trillion,

asr-001419
01:46:28.600 --> 01:46:33.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: enabling them to implement priority programs and projects nationwide.

asr-001420
01:46:33.600 --> 01:46:36.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But even as NGAs receive the largest nominal share,

asr-001421
01:46:36.600 --> 01:46:40.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: their allocation grows by only 4.5%,

asr-001422
01:46:40.600 --> 01:46:44.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: below the overall 6% growth of the national budget,

asr-001423
01:46:44.600 --> 01:46:48.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: again reflecting restraint in national government spending.

asr-001424
01:46:48.600 --> 01:46:53.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Local government units will receive P1.533 trillion,

asr-001425
01:46:53.600 --> 01:46:57.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: recognizing their critical role in delivering frontline services

asr-001426
01:46:57.600 --> 01:47:01.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and responding to the needs of local communities.

asr-001427
01:47:01.600 --> 01:47:06.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: A major component is the P1.32 trillion NTA,

asr-001428
01:47:06.600 --> 01:47:11.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: compared with around P1.191 trillion this year,

asr-001429
01:47:11.600 --> 01:47:16.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: an increase of roughly P129.3 billion

asr-001430
01:47:16.600 --> 01:47:21.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: flowing directly to our local government units.

asr-001431
01:47:21.600 --> 01:47:26.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We have also provided P220.5 billion for GOCCs

asr-001432
01:47:26.600 --> 01:47:31.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and P1.14 trillion for interest payments.

asr-001433
01:47:31.600 --> 01:47:35.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This distribution shows that the budget is not concentrated

asr-001434
01:47:35.600 --> 01:47:37.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: solely in the national bureaucracy.

asr-001435
01:47:37.600 --> 01:47:42.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: A substantial and growing amount is being transferred to the local level

asr-001436
01:47:42.600 --> 01:47:48.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: where many government services are actually delivered to our citizens.

asr-001437
01:47:48.600 --> 01:47:50.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This brings us to another important dimension

asr-001438
01:47:50.600 --> 01:47:53.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of the budget, where the money will go.

asr-001439
01:47:53.600 --> 01:47:57.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Of the proposed fiscal year 2027 national budget,

asr-001440
01:47:57.600 --> 01:48:04.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: P4.603 trillion or 63.9% will be directly allocated

asr-001441
01:48:04.600 --> 01:48:07.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to the regions to support programs and projects

asr-001442
01:48:07.600 --> 01:48:10.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: responsive to local development priorities.

asr-001443
01:48:10.600 --> 01:48:15.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Of this amount, National Capital Region will receive P1.112 trillion,

asr-001444
01:48:15.600 --> 01:48:19.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Luzon at P1.659 trillion,

asr-001445
01:48:19.600 --> 01:48:23.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Visayas at P744.8 billion,

asr-001446
01:48:23.600 --> 01:48:27.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and Mindanao at P1.088 trillion.

asr-001447
01:48:27.600 --> 01:48:33.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The remaining 36.1% or P2.597 trillion

asr-001448
01:48:33.600 --> 01:48:36.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: constitutes the non-regionalized budget.

asr-001449
01:48:36.600 --> 01:48:39.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This consists of nationwide allocations

asr-001450
01:48:39.600 --> 01:48:45.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: amounting to P1.983 trillion or 27.5%

asr-001451
01:48:45.600 --> 01:48:48.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and central office allocations totaling

asr-001452
01:48:48.600 --> 01:48:52.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to P213.8 billion or 8.5%.

asr-001453
01:48:52.600 --> 01:48:56.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But nationwide should not be mistaken for Metro Manila.

asr-001454
01:48:56.600 --> 01:49:00.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: These include resources that will eventually benefit regions

asr-001455
01:49:00.600 --> 01:49:03.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and beneficiaries across the country

asr-001456
01:49:03.600 --> 01:49:06.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: but cannot yet be geographically assigned

asr-001457
01:49:06.600 --> 01:49:08.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: at the time the NEP is prepared.

asr-001458
01:49:08.600 --> 01:49:11.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The broader direction is that the majority of the budget

asr-001459
01:49:11.600 --> 01:49:14.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is intended to reach our regions and communities.

asr-001460
01:49:14.600 --> 01:49:16.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This is what we mean when we say

asr-001461
01:49:16.600 --> 01:49:20.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Bawat Bayan Makikinabang.

asr-001462
01:49:20.600 --> 01:49:24.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: With the overall framework and dimensions of the budget laid out,

asr-001463
01:49:24.600 --> 01:49:29.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: let us now look more closely at where some of our biggest investments will go.

asr-001464
01:49:29.600 --> 01:49:33.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The Department of Education will receive the highest allocation

asr-001465
01:49:33.600 --> 01:49:36.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: at P975.96 billion,

asr-001466
01:49:36.600 --> 01:49:39.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: affirming the government's enduring commitment

asr-001467
01:49:39.600 --> 01:49:41.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to investing in our people.

asr-001468
01:49:41.600 --> 01:49:43.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But beyond basic education,

asr-001469
01:49:43.600 --> 01:49:45.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the proposed budget allocates

asr-001470
01:49:45.600 --> 01:49:50.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: P176.5 billion for higher education

asr-001471
01:49:50.600 --> 01:49:53.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to ensure that more Filipinos have access to quality

asr-001472
01:49:53.600 --> 01:49:56.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and affordable tertiary education.

asr-001473
01:49:56.600 --> 01:50:01.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Altogether, the proposed investment in basic and higher education

asr-001474
01:50:01.600 --> 01:50:04.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: amounts to P1.326 trillion,

asr-001475
01:50:04.600 --> 01:50:07.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: equivalent to nearly 4% of GDP,

asr-001476
01:50:07.600 --> 01:50:10.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: effectively reaching the lower bound

asr-001477
01:50:10.600 --> 01:50:13.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of the UNESCO Education 2030 benchmark

asr-001478
01:50:13.600 --> 01:50:15.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of 4-6%.

asr-001479
01:50:15.600 --> 01:50:22.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Within these totals are very concrete investments.

asr-001480
01:50:22.600 --> 01:50:25.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are proposing P12.09 billion

asr-001481
01:50:25.600 --> 01:50:28.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for the expanded career progression system

asr-001482
01:50:28.600 --> 01:50:30.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for public school teachers,

asr-001483
01:50:30.600 --> 01:50:34.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: nearly double the fiscal year 2026 level,

asr-001484
01:50:34.600 --> 01:50:36.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to support the reclassification

asr-001485
01:50:36.600 --> 01:50:39.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and career advancement of our teachers.

asr-001486
01:50:39.600 --> 01:50:44.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This reflects an increase of P5.94 billion

asr-001487
01:50:44.600 --> 01:50:50.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: or 96.6% from the fiscal year 2026 level.

asr-001488
01:50:50.600 --> 01:50:53.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are providing P10.36 billion

asr-001489
01:50:53.600 --> 01:50:55.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for the teaching allowance,

asr-001490
01:50:55.600 --> 01:50:59.600
